#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382757 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152197 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "99c2db8c-670b-521b-8942-3b89f1e95d3f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Injections For Functions Whose Domain or Codomain Are Real Intervals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bf5d37a-6a00-5f10-8c55-9bbf970be92f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453156} {:answer/id #uuid "7aabeaaa-3849-5d13-a1f9-585d16f30b83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453157}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7aabeaaa-3849-5d13-a1f9-585d16f30b83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453157} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d09a131-c0e0-5472-9310-cb6dc878fd2b" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454328} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a6a85fcb-471d-59b8-8bbf-b61ac06e8c71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453158} {:answer/id #uuid "42f1bfb9-3ee8-576b-8d94-62e4e82fe7a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453159}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a6a85fcb-471d-59b8-8bbf-b61ac06e8c71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453158} :answer-field/id #uuid "858a3d04-ac8a-53d5-a5f5-9dc8ece2494a" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454329} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4785ad13-bddb-53ce-98ae-ef532d0b5549" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453160} {:answer/id #uuid "43d8aafb-36cd-57c5-ae2b-29091b7a792b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453161}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "43d8aafb-36cd-57c5-ae2b-29091b7a792b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453161} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c4e34de-81f1-556d-93cf-cdcb98a4c2df" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454330}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b0c99dc3-deba-5ffb-83d8-510a75eea6dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-105206" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:[-2,2]\\to R$ which is given by $f(x)=\\frac{1}{2}({x}^{3}-x)?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $f(-1)=f(1)$\n- **II.** $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in [-2,2],$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$\n- **III.** $f$ is not **one-to-one**" :question/worked-solution "First, we graph the function.\n\n![](images/86/869be2ef6cb317b81c249b85b0afcbea23178dcf3bb77bb008e69375494439df.png)\n\nA function $f:X\\to Y$ is an injection (also known as *one-to-one*) if *every* element in $X$ is mapped to a *distinct* element in $Y:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. We have $f(-1)=\\frac{1}{2}((-1)^{3}-(-1))=0$ and $f(1)=\\frac{1}{2}({1}^{3}-1)=0.$\n\n- Statement II is false. We have $f(-1)=f(1)$ but $-1\\ne 1.$ So, it's *not true* that for all ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ contained within the domain $[-2,2],$ if $f({x}_{1})$ and $f({x}_{2})$ are equal, then we must have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, since statement II is false, $f$ is not an injection (also known as *one-to-one*).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383466 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162153 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "196e7d31-5af8-5c82-b2bd-0cf1ed7415e2" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Random Variables are Independent Given the Joint PMF Only"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b7c73a6-2af0-5b92-b6f9-3d93e71ac279" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453410} {:answer/id #uuid "cd588ae9-2b60-5171-90a5-e75b1b1f4e4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453411}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd588ae9-2b60-5171-90a5-e75b1b1f4e4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453411} :answer-field/id #uuid "e212ea0e-0893-522d-b146-c4a56808a680" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454455} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f3e69a34-93a1-5a43-834c-4e189751c4d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453412} {:answer/id #uuid "2d4c23a1-a357-5eb9-9f99-65ce1db5f659" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453413}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2d4c23a1-a357-5eb9-9f99-65ce1db5f659" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453413} :answer-field/id #uuid "79de55e8-6943-548b-a367-c214c3149889" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454456} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f17d2094-f158-54e5-846d-74fedf6ed19e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453414} {:answer/id #uuid "68e664fb-4f6e-51e7-b3d4-8922d50069a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453415}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "68e664fb-4f6e-51e7-b3d4-8922d50069a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453415} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ed06e01-142b-5c2b-b22f-d3c32e2dbb48" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454457}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "47bb5e3d-7de9-53ad-b629-7512a9b347ce" :question/math-academy-id "q-143328" :question/problem "The joint probability distribution $f(x,y)$ of the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given below. \n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.3$ | $0.45$ |\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $P(X=1,Y=2)=P(X=1)\\cdot P(Y=2)$\n- **II.** $P(X=x,Y=y)=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$\n- **III.** $X$ and $Y$ are independent" :question/worked-solution "Two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with a joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ are independent if and only if \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)\n$$\n\n \n\nfor all possible values $x$ and $y,$ where ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal probability mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nComputing the marginal probability mass functions for  $X$ and $Y,$ we obtain the following:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ | $0.25$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.3$ | $0.45$ | $0.75$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.4$ | $0.6$ | $1$ |\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. From the table, we obtain that $P(X=1,Y=2)=f(1,2)=0.15.$ On the other hand, \n\n$$\nP(X=1)\\cdot P(Y=2)={f}_{X}(1)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(2)=0.25\\cdot 0.6=0.15.\\,✓\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Checking all other possible products, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1,1) & =0.1=0.25\\cdot 0.4={f}_{X}(1)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(1) & ✓ \\\\ f(2,1) & =0.3=0.75\\cdot 0.4={f}_{X}(2)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(1) & ✓ \\\\ f(2,2) & =0.45=0.75\\cdot 0.6={f}_{X}(2)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(2) & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $P(X=x,Y=y)=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is true, our random variables $X$ and $Y$ must be independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383561 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198400 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4179839d-85c4-5325-9293-e332bd209597" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Inverse Function Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e3abbc8c-d671-5959-b597-abe008d06807" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453484} {:answer/id #uuid "0b13cfd9-8f9a-5bc4-b62e-9acf0c9835c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453485}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e3abbc8c-d671-5959-b597-abe008d06807" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453484} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e82a4ca-4e2a-5f53-9d73-7e8509121373" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454492} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c2343d7-3f2b-5c50-b87e-7d948c13e525" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453486} {:answer/id #uuid "1f220f7b-6094-53ec-b07a-bbddab98f505" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453487}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1f220f7b-6094-53ec-b07a-bbddab98f505" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453487} :answer-field/id #uuid "d93fb9b1-7a78-5650-bb54-3504271bf9eb" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454493} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fa16e892-8ac0-5080-820e-607b8aff0a31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453488} {:answer/id #uuid "5b95beb1-056f-56f2-9817-32b180ee6f10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453489}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5b95beb1-056f-56f2-9817-32b180ee6f10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453489} :answer-field/id #uuid "50770a0c-f153-535c-bc5d-43b6e01324e9" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454494}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "61853900-8f46-5757-9fa9-7e0c887a8b65" :question/math-academy-id "q-161849" :question/problem "Let $f:U\\to R$ be continuously differentiable on an open set $U⊆R$ such that $f(a)=b$ and ${f}^{′}(a)\\ne 0$ for $a\\in U.$ Which of the following statements **must** be true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The function $f$ is invertible on $U.$\n- **II.** The inverse ${f}^{-1}$ is continuously differentiable in a neighborhood of $b.$\n- **III.** The derivative of ${f}^{-1}$ is given by ${({f}^{-1})}^{′}(b)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(a)}.$" :question/worked-solution "The inverse function theorem for single-variable functions states the following:\n\n*If $f:U\\to R$ is continuously differentiable on an open set $U⊆R,$ $f(a)=b$ and ${f}^{′}(a)\\ne 0$ for $a\\in U,$ then*\n\n- *$f$ is invertible in some neighborhood of $a,$*\n\n- *${f}^{-1},$ the inverse of $f,$ is continuously differentiable in a neighborhood of $b,$ and*\n\n- *the derivative of ${f}^{-1}$ is given by* \n\n$$\n{({f}^{-1})}^{′}(b)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(a)}=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(b))}\\,.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. According to the theorem, the function $f$ must be invertible in some neighborhood of $a,$ which could be smaller than $U.$ \n\nFor example, the function $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ satisfies the conditions of the inverse function theorem for $U=(0,\\pi )$ and $a=\\frac{\\pi }{4}.$ However, $f(x)$ is not invertible on the entire set $U,$ only on a subset of $U.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, the inverse ${f}^{-1}$ must be continuously differentiable in a neighborhood of $b.$\n\n- Statement III is true. According to the theorem, we must have ${({f}^{-1})}^{′}(b)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(a)}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383687 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054640 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d4954fe5-f1fe-590a-9540-280a14606a49" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aaa3babe-fc8a-5abc-bbf5-d3767d792f6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453616} {:answer/id #uuid "c1e55f60-ad7a-5563-b5e2-159c439a70ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453617}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aaa3babe-fc8a-5abc-bbf5-d3767d792f6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453616} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d7fdab7-f983-5bc2-bb04-1f895b807dfb" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454558} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "de45af91-7568-5e47-b37f-4413eeae542d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453618} {:answer/id #uuid "710b6a64-0fde-520e-acb4-e44ce684997e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453619}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "de45af91-7568-5e47-b37f-4413eeae542d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453618} :answer-field/id #uuid "c726e020-da13-5ea6-bafe-4ed894d72a26" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454559} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a1d878aa-3421-5025-86bd-8a47672bae55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453620} {:answer/id #uuid "84aca991-7429-5390-ab6f-fd636bcc8a7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453621}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "84aca991-7429-5390-ab6f-fd636bcc8a7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453621} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd9eceba-08ff-5052-86b4-313736cb0156" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454560}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a540711c-ecf6-55f0-99c0-da5fdfa24e62" :question/math-academy-id "q-182224" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $P(∅)={∅,{∅}}$\n- **II.** $P({a,∅})={∅,{a},{a,∅}}$\n- **III.** $P({∅})={∅,{∅}}$" :question/worked-solution "The power set of $T,$ denoted $P(T),$ is the set that contains every possible subset of $T,$ including the empty set $∅.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. Notice that we are given the set $∅.$ So, its power set must be ${∅}.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Notice that we are given the set ${a,∅}.$ So, its power set must be ${∅,{a},{∅},{a,∅}}.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, the power set of the set ${∅}$ is ${∅,{∅}}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385631 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152265 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f237343d-2f8a-5a9f-9e5f-c9f22784547a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Bijections For Functions Functions Defined Algebraically"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a40aa1f8-3059-5f5c-b4f4-a4957bb527ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453958} {:answer/id #uuid "fa8a0314-af7a-533f-8842-eafbbfc3f11b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453959}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa8a0314-af7a-533f-8842-eafbbfc3f11b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453959} :answer-field/id #uuid "01c07248-5ea7-5a73-b9e1-aa1ef9790d17" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454729} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3fa36298-c254-5ae7-9f57-6e21928b62aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453960} {:answer/id #uuid "3530d61c-a4fb-52d2-b8da-3ead200044aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453961}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3fa36298-c254-5ae7-9f57-6e21928b62aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453960} :answer-field/id #uuid "17ba2f9a-6d44-522e-9646-4c379db01776" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454730} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eeae9ef8-5d24-5c8a-bb5d-85d9ffc8052b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453962} {:answer/id #uuid "0ac8ebfc-3801-5252-b2b8-555ad3e72b32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453963}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eeae9ef8-5d24-5c8a-bb5d-85d9ffc8052b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453962} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab404ed8-bd98-5c3f-aadf-e57c714907e0" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454731}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d499a969-2317-5182-b93d-3971b580fa67" :question/math-academy-id "q-76260" :question/problem "For the function $f:Q\\to R$ defined by $f(x)={x}^{3},$ which of the following  statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The function is an injection\n- **II.** The function is a surjection\n- **III.** The function is a bijection" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a function $f:X\\to Y$ is \n\n- an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ whenever $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2},$\n\n- a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y,$\n\n- a bijection if it is both a surjection and an injection.\n\nWith this in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f({x}_{1}) & =f({x}_{2}) \\\\ {x}_{1}^{3} & ={x}_{2}^{3} \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{{x}_{1}^{3}} & =\\sqrt[3]{{x}_{2}^{3}} \\\\ {x}_{1} & ={x}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. As a counterexample, choose $2\\in R.$ There is no number $x\\in Q$ such that $f(x)=2.$ The only number $x$ that satisfies ${x}^{3}=2$ is $x=\\sqrt[3]{2}\\notin Q.$\n\n- Statement III is false because the function is not a surjection.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385713 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152196 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a347133c-5e5a-5dd2-89ef-bdd14245ee6b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Injections For Functions Defined on the Set of Real Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f3007f3c-e5d9-54ac-acb1-fed4d2df4b2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454036} {:answer/id #uuid "24a7f90e-4c9f-5e9b-bcfa-dd14f93bf09a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454037}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f3007f3c-e5d9-54ac-acb1-fed4d2df4b2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454036} :answer-field/id #uuid "55403f69-b0a5-5b52-8781-9406fcd48ea3" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454768} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "76861d48-ff1a-57b6-a42d-3d2fd72ba212" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454038} {:answer/id #uuid "45b76c31-a794-5780-9602-0a7c9868204b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454039}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "45b76c31-a794-5780-9602-0a7c9868204b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454039} :answer-field/id #uuid "b52bd5c3-60b8-54c4-916e-f386fc023174" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454769} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ced0fb16-8404-5b66-b796-6c626b0afbdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454040} {:answer/id #uuid "23bf899e-b083-56f2-8bdd-325f6c57396f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454041}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "23bf899e-b083-56f2-8bdd-325f6c57396f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454041} :answer-field/id #uuid "9568da31-5657-5c24-abdd-6d98e31cae5d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454770}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b7872e3a-407b-5f7a-81c4-4f36c9894a9b" :question/math-academy-id "q-80378" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:R\\to R$ which is given by $f(x)=3-{x}^{3}?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $f(-3)=f(0)$\n- **II.** $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$\n- **III.** $f$ is **one-to-one**" :question/worked-solution "First, we graph the function.\n\n![](images/44/44a0d65bb3fc4f090dc82acc36a5c4657acaf5f9c8b0b80fe0a2cc30a3ac61e2.png)\n\nA function $f:X\\to Y$ is an injection (also known as *one-to-one*) if *every* element in $X$ is mapped to a *distinct* element in $Y:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. We have $f(-3)=3-(-3)^{3}=30$ and $f(0)=3-{0}^{3}=3.$\n\n- Statement II is true. As we can see from the graph, it passes the horizontal line test, meaning that there are no two distinct elements within $R$ that map to the same element in $R.$ So, for all ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ contained within the domain $R,$ if $f({x}_{1})$ and $f({x}_{2})$ are equal, then we must have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, since statement II is true, $f$ is an injection (also known as *one-to-one*).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385720 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152197 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "99c2db8c-670b-521b-8942-3b89f1e95d3f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Injections For Functions Whose Domain or Codomain Are Real Intervals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d6f8b72e-897c-5e0d-92c3-ac73a0f28a75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454042} {:answer/id #uuid "a76df206-0026-5aaf-81c5-975f9295aec2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454043}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a76df206-0026-5aaf-81c5-975f9295aec2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454043} :answer-field/id #uuid "a059fc80-3508-58b8-90cd-44eaf28b2ce6" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454771} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "508bcc28-61d9-5a0b-a2d8-3396206b5312" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454044} {:answer/id #uuid "4586401f-787c-5e65-b2da-5a61f7b41aab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454045}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "508bcc28-61d9-5a0b-a2d8-3396206b5312" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454044} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d51ad1e-feb1-5643-b5ea-276c808f8a3b" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454772} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14f9f25f-46eb-51ab-9f54-b52c158c6ea0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454046} {:answer/id #uuid "96f218d4-0928-5de2-b331-75fa2971a3c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454047}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "14f9f25f-46eb-51ab-9f54-b52c158c6ea0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454046} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f51fddc-87f3-5da4-be10-651497ab82ad" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454773}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d7f30a04-d85b-56f5-8c95-f8906883e6fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-80386" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:[-2,1]\\to R$ which is given by $f(x)={x}^{3}+{x}^{2}?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $f(-1)=f(0)$\n- **II.** $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in [-2,1],$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$\n- **III.** $f$ is **one-to-one**" :question/worked-solution "First, we graph the function.\n\n![](images/a0/a0e70acd2c7844de100c5c0cb0f85480af17921308b23d505b7ea639ce4690b9.png)\n\nA function $f:X\\to Y$ is an injection (also known as *one-to-one*) if *every* element in $X$ is mapped to a *distinct* element in $Y:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. We have $f(-1)=(-1)^{3}+(-1)^{2}=0$ and $f(0)=0.$\n\n- Statement II is false. We have $f(-1)=f(0)$ but $-1\\ne 0.$ So, it's *not true* that for all ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ contained within the domain $[-2,1],$ if $f({x}_{1})$ and $f({x}_{2})$ are equal, then we must have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Indeed, since statement II is false, $f$ is not an injection (also known as *one-to-one*).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385803 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152265 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f237343d-2f8a-5a9f-9e5f-c9f22784547a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Bijections For Functions Functions Defined Algebraically"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c1d22ff0-d65c-5ada-a9d6-2abf4c5625a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454072} {:answer/id #uuid "b2994bfa-b394-5f16-8b51-2743837eba99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454073}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b2994bfa-b394-5f16-8b51-2743837eba99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454073} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e3a7e2c-6095-532e-9df6-ac3844ce7b49" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454786} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d01a3361-56d5-5718-91e2-901eda2487c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454074} {:answer/id #uuid "1c8fcb79-82e9-5077-ab31-8f8bde4e1a9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454075}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d01a3361-56d5-5718-91e2-901eda2487c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454074} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4c41118-b50a-5deb-a97a-8d1bc552bc67" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454787} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49a8178b-e2ee-5b6a-aed8-c5441cf79aa5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454076} {:answer/id #uuid "e346a0cb-8c92-55fa-9bfc-a2e9318b2fb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454077}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "49a8178b-e2ee-5b6a-aed8-c5441cf79aa5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454076} :answer-field/id #uuid "86eb81be-6c39-5f8e-a2e3-95bfdafc0e2b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454788}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "fc152a7c-fa1b-52cf-a24e-e996a44c8d98" :question/math-academy-id "q-82325" :question/problem "For the function $f:Q\\to R$ defined by $f(x)=\\sqrt[3]{x},$ which of the following  statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The function is an injection\n- **II.** The function is a surjection\n- **III.** The function is a bijection" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a function $f:X\\to Y$ is \n\n- an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ whenever $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2},$\n\n- a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y,$\n\n- a bijection if it is both a surjection and an injection.\n\nWith this in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f({x}_{1}) & =f({x}_{2}) \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{{x}_{1}} & =\\sqrt[3]{{x}_{2}} \\\\ {(\\sqrt[3]{{x}_{1}})}^{3} & ={(\\sqrt[3]{{x}_{2}})}^{3} \\\\ {x}_{1} & ={x}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. As a counterexample, choose $\\sqrt{2}\\in R.$ There is no number $x\\in Q$ such that $f(x)=\\sqrt{2}.$ The only number $x$ that satisfies $\\sqrt[3]{x}=\\sqrt{2}$ is $x=\\sqrt{8}=2\\sqrt{2}\\notin Q.$ Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\sqrt[3]{\\sqrt{8}}={({2}^{3/2})}^{1/3}={2}^{1/2}=\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false because the function is not a surjection.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406841 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188273 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e12609b7-286b-50a8-8373-a331d60ab904" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Using the Rank-Nullity Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f8f9232e-9658-51ed-95f2-ac2fd1e78bf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454078} {:answer/id #uuid "a2a49195-0754-59e8-a736-789d713df706" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454079}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a2a49195-0754-59e8-a736-789d713df706" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454079} :answer-field/id #uuid "3fee3505-d7fb-511a-a74e-2a2d44598ed9" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454789} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33b58ec5-18ed-565a-8a4c-7a428ef3b660" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454080} {:answer/id #uuid "fa80fb0a-3883-56b5-b6eb-070e8e31d145" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454081}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "33b58ec5-18ed-565a-8a4c-7a428ef3b660" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454080} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d6a4961-38f7-5264-b58e-a39849428f01" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454790} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "642014a7-57ea-5677-bbda-439505c688fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454082} {:answer/id #uuid "fbeac619-768a-5b27-a0a3-6f578395c470" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454083}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "642014a7-57ea-5677-bbda-439505c688fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454082} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0f9063c-3f2e-5e1f-893e-6358b44768be" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454791}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "838322c6-867e-5a73-a18d-bbf81bd1218b" :question/math-academy-id "q-84081" :question/problem "Let $T:{R}^{3}\\to {R}^{3}$ be a linear transformation whose standard matrix is $T.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** If $\\text{Ker}(T)={[x,y,z]^{T}\\,:\\,y=z=0}$ then $\\text{rank}(T)=2$\n- **II.** If $Tx=[1,0,0]^{T}$ has more than one solution, then $\\text{nullity}(T)=0$\n- **III.** If $\\text{Ker}(T)=\\text{Span}{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}$, then $T$ is invertible" :question/worked-solution "Since $T$ is a linear transformation from ${R}^{3}$ into ${R}^{3},$ the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n $T$ is a bijection (an invertible transformation) $\\,⟺\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Im}(T)={R}^{3} \\\\  & \\text{rank}(T)=3 \\\\  & \\text{Ker}(T)={0} \\\\  & \\text{nullity}(T)=0\\end{aligned}$ \n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(T)+\\text{nullity}(T)=3.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Since $y=z=0,$ any vector from $\\text{Ker}(T)$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=x{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{v}_{1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that $\\text{Ker}(T)=\\text{Span}{{v}_{1}}.$ Therefore, $\\text{nullity}(T)=1.$ Finally, according the rank-nullity theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(T) & =3-\\text{nullity}(T) \\\\  & =3-1 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $Tx=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ has more than one solution, there are ${u}_{1},{u}_{2}\\in {R}^{3}$ such that  ${u}_{1}\\ne {u}_{2}$ and \n\n$$\nT({u}_{1})=T({u}_{2})=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis means, $T$ is not a bijection and according to the invertible matrix theorem, $\\text{nullity}(T)\\ne 0.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Notice that $\\text{Ker}(T)=\\text{Span}{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}.$ Therefore, $\\text{nullity}(T)=1.$ So, $T$ is not a bijection or, which is the same, $T$ is not invertible.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406880 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124490 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ca956d3e-37a8-5f0f-a062-97d0567d54e6" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Bases of Abstract Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f0fb2451-4145-52a4-a863-c1c6b500c031" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454178} {:answer/id #uuid "52bf72c1-2d03-54f1-83ce-0080cfe75fc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454179}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f0fb2451-4145-52a4-a863-c1c6b500c031" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454178} :answer-field/id #uuid "03f577e9-d7b5-59b1-9054-aeaecadbcd8d" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454839} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6291cb58-5945-57e8-971a-03bf17a20742" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454180} {:answer/id #uuid "e330a199-18c6-573a-b614-26a3494d9178" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454181}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6291cb58-5945-57e8-971a-03bf17a20742" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454180} :answer-field/id #uuid "e630bf03-420c-549c-8c6a-4ca716a3ea03" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454840} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b7df072b-200d-5d6c-a18b-7f91a1928602" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454182} {:answer/id #uuid "2454f33d-1680-5c05-9fc3-08394323c4ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454183}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2454f33d-1680-5c05-9fc3-08394323c4ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454183} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8f08f4c-963a-5572-927c-4df8af138eba" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454841}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1d66ed66-f11f-53c8-af0e-1883d2bbdd40" :question/math-academy-id "q-94942" :question/problem "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}$ be a basis of a vector space $V.$ \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3},w}$ is linearly independent\n- **II.** ${{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ is linearly dependent\n- **III.** ${{b}_{1},3{b}_{2},2{b}_{3}}$ is a basis of $V$" :question/worked-solution "Since $B$ is a basis, the following properties must hold:\n\n- $B$ is a maximally linearly independent set of vectors in $V,$ and\n\n- $B$ spans $V.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. Since $B$ is a basis of $V,$ it is a maximally linearly independent set of vectors. This means that if we add any new vector to the set, it becomes linearly dependent.\n\n- Statement II is false. Since if ${{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ is linearly dependent then there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}=0,\n$$\n\nwhere at least one of $x$'s is not zero. But then \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+0{b}_{3}=0,\n$$\n\nwhich would mean that $B$ is linearly dependent. This would contradict the fact that $B$ is a basis.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}(3{b}_{2})+{x}_{3}(2{b}_{3}) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+(3{x}_{2}){b}_{2}+(2{x}_{3}){b}_{3} & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich, since ${{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}$ is linearly independent, gives\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{3}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, ${{b}_{1},3{b}_{2},2{b}_{3}}$ spans $V$ since any linear combination of vectors from $B$ can be expressed as a linear combination of ${{b}_{1},3{b}_{2},2{b}_{3}}:$\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+{x}_{3}{b}_{3}={x}_{1}{b}_{1}+\\frac{{x}_{2}}{3}(3{b}_{2})+\\frac{{x}_{3}}{2}(2{b}_{3})\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406881 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124489 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "073042ee-d96d-5872-9681-ddcea43a2d37" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Sets of Vectors in a Matrix Vector Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aaaf8ce1-2c2b-5bcc-925e-0f599acad60d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454172} {:answer/id #uuid "c647dd27-09cc-5bd3-810e-1d4746a2941e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454173}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c647dd27-09cc-5bd3-810e-1d4746a2941e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454173} :answer-field/id #uuid "619d8289-a96c-58c5-9ea1-3220d6f4efec" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454836} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6aa5580c-81c0-5f4c-a754-31a21c559398" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454174} {:answer/id #uuid "0bb76b41-f895-5d96-b445-577e31e07b34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454175}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0bb76b41-f895-5d96-b445-577e31e07b34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454175} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa0354d6-0d92-52da-b49b-f1f1344babb1" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454837} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "de933d44-9208-5817-bc6e-9512bd25a83a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454176} {:answer/id #uuid "5c945b34-ae4d-5fc2-b49a-c1b5910f20d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454177}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "de933d44-9208-5817-bc6e-9512bd25a83a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454176} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd8df321-1ba8-5043-8b63-8be3125b1692" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454838}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "455cce4b-aebd-5209-87a1-ec6ed81f2e6b" :question/math-academy-id "q-94867" :question/problem "Consider the vector space ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ of all $2\\times 2$ matrices over $R.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\}$ is a linearly independent set in ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$\n\n- **II.** $[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]$ can be expressed as a linear combination of $\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\}$\n\n- **III.** $\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\}$ is a basis of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis true if and only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$ So, the set is linearly independent.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]=2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]+(-4)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]+3\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. For example, the matrix $[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ can't be written as a linear combination of \n\n$$\n\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\}\n$$\n\nsince all these linear combinations result in matrices with the entry ${a}_{21}=0:$\n\n$$\na\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]+b\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]+c\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}a & c \\\\ 0 & b\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406882 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124489 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "073042ee-d96d-5872-9681-ddcea43a2d37" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Sets of Vectors in a Matrix Vector Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "69e86229-681b-5403-b631-b065124b1be8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453234} {:answer/id #uuid "e78110f0-ca50-51aa-914f-e386bec6425a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453235}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e78110f0-ca50-51aa-914f-e386bec6425a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453235} :answer-field/id #uuid "4cbdc373-c990-5dd3-8186-7aa74bd3bb9d" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454367} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cfdf83a2-6a63-5759-a053-db246c627b2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453236} {:answer/id #uuid "aa9113d9-1b88-5970-a100-85c7aea2dbff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453237}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa9113d9-1b88-5970-a100-85c7aea2dbff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453237} :answer-field/id #uuid "195daa73-27ff-5877-a458-d22d5ed1852b" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454368} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2fd8a2c9-e002-5140-8dcb-a07eb82acf68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453238} {:answer/id #uuid "c6c0ea91-328a-544b-b2c0-d0c461ef46cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453239}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c6c0ea91-328a-544b-b2c0-d0c461ef46cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453239} :answer-field/id #uuid "9796340d-a680-530e-86de-58d047300c0a" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454369}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5b0d7b89-c3c8-5cee-b6a2-01b5cd1b1f67" :question/math-academy-id "q-107533" :question/problem "Consider the vector space ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ of all $2\\times 2$ matrices over $R.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\}$ is a linearly independent set in ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$\n\n- **II.** $[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -5\\end{aligned}]$ can be expressed as a linear combination of $\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\}$\n\n- **III.** $\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\}$ is a basis of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{4}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis true if and only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}={x}_{4}=0.$ So, the set is linearly independent.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -5\\end{aligned}]=3\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]+(-4)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]+(-2)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]+(-5)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, the set is linearly independent and for any matrix in ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R),$ we get \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}]=a\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]+(-b)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]+(-c)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]+d\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406883 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124490 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ca956d3e-37a8-5f0f-a062-97d0567d54e6" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Bases of Abstract Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8bbdee2f-94bd-572f-91ae-a989e989cefc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454060} {:answer/id #uuid "ad6016de-8322-5611-abac-11c53498b5f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454061}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8bbdee2f-94bd-572f-91ae-a989e989cefc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454060} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b86c8c7-ce4a-5843-b124-fd92dc984de2" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454780} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e5061063-49ba-56ef-8537-f424f6dc8a16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454062} {:answer/id #uuid "710153ca-da8e-5423-9cbc-1f6713a46398" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454063}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "710153ca-da8e-5423-9cbc-1f6713a46398" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454063} :answer-field/id #uuid "a7647c92-3c6a-55d5-b2a1-537c5b726446" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454781} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0743a148-5538-58b8-be74-ca107d1c906d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454064} {:answer/id #uuid "f3c81ac2-78b7-59ca-8a48-01ff07cdd26a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454065}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0743a148-5538-58b8-be74-ca107d1c906d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454064} :answer-field/id #uuid "ccfdb226-5087-511e-8a84-93a1b34f530a" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454782}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b3557614-de80-516a-bb07-7b50ae99a56a" :question/math-academy-id "q-80631" :question/problem "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}$ and $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2}}$ are bases of ${R}^{3}$ and ${R}^{2}$, respectively. \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${x,{b}_{2},{c}_{1}}$ is a basis of ${R}^{3}$\n- **II.** ${-2{b}_{3},3{b}_{1},5{b}_{2}}$ is a basis of ${R}^{3}$\n- **III.** ${{c}_{1},{c}_{2},x}$ is a basis of ${R}^{2}$" :question/worked-solution "Since $B$ and $C$ are bases, the following properties must hold:\n\n- $B$ and $C$ are maximally linearly independent sets in ${R}^{2}$ and ${R}^{3},$ respectively, and\n\n- $B$ spans ${R}^{2},$ while $C$ spans ${R}^{3}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. The set ${x,{b}_{2},{c}_{1}}$ is not a basis of ${R}^{3}$ because the set contains vectors from another vector space.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(-2{b}_{3})+{x}_{2}(3{b}_{1})+{x}_{3}(5{b}_{2}) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-2{x}_{1}){b}_{3}+(3{x}_{2}){b}_{1}+(5{x}_{3}){b}_{2} & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich, since ${{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}$ is linearly independent, gives\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{1}=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 5{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{3}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, ${-2{b}_{3},3{b}_{1},5{b}_{2}}$ spans $V$ since any linear combination of vectors from $B$ can be expressed as a linear combination of ${-2{b}_{3},3{b}_{1},5{b}_{2}}:$\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+{x}_{3}{b}_{3}=\\frac{{x}_{1}}{3}(3{b}_{1})+\\frac{{x}_{2}}{5}(5{b}_{2})+(-\\frac{{x}_{3}}{2})(-2{b}_{3})\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2}}$ is a basis of ${R}^{2}$, any vector of ${R}^{2},$ including the given vector $x,$ can be written as a linear combination of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}.$ This means that ${{c}_{1},{c}_{2},x}$ is linearly dependent and therefore, cannot be a basis.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406949 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059701 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "64a3922f-7e74-562f-9bb9-c4a41e912ce7" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Conditional Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a11b4773-38d5-5c0c-9e9c-3e0b4ecae818" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453132} {:answer/id #uuid "9ab874b5-03d7-53c3-b6db-a652d9c156a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453133}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a11b4773-38d5-5c0c-9e9c-3e0b4ecae818" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453132} :answer-field/id #uuid "26f8e36a-498b-5385-816f-6d262d6c4893" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454316} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "96553132-07aa-5dd8-a9d9-80d5ba1e0f0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453134} {:answer/id #uuid "f12b50d9-97e8-547c-ae5c-e9776f0678cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453135}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f12b50d9-97e8-547c-ae5c-e9776f0678cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453135} :answer-field/id #uuid "cae81137-1867-50f5-a1a9-e15ecfd57220" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454317} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "923f9c82-2491-5942-a700-0059eb11d931" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453136} {:answer/id #uuid "bca078d7-e26d-5c8c-ac29-1d2b30f25905" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453137}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bca078d7-e26d-5c8c-ac29-1d2b30f25905" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453137} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8ffb718-a2da-578a-a502-45fd1b77e827" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454318}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "55e540af-11e2-5ec3-9b47-ab0da3ac740e" :question/math-academy-id "q-103558" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** **If** $12$ is divisible by $3$, **then** $9$ is divisible by $4.$\n- **II.** **If** $5$ is divisible by $2$, **then** $10$ is divisible by $5.$\n- **III.** **If** $9$ is divisible by $5$, **then** $6$ is divisible by $3.$" :question/worked-solution "An implication $A⇒B$ is true *unless* $A$ is true and $B$ is false. In other words, the implication is true unless the \"promise\" is broken.\n\n- Statement I is false. The antecedent \"$12$ is divisible by $3$\" is true, and the consequent \"$9$ is divisible by $4$\" is false. So the promise is broken, and the statement is false.\n\n- Statement II is true. The antecedent \"$5$ is divisible by $2$\" is false, so the promise does not apply. Regardless of the consequent, the promise is *not* broken, and the statement is true.\n\n- Statement III is true. Again, the antecedent \"$9$ is divisible by $5$\" is false, so the promise does not apply. Regardless of the consequent, the promise is *not* broken, and the statement is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406950 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059701 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "64a3922f-7e74-562f-9bb9-c4a41e912ce7" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Conditional Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20959140-93b8-5a47-a197-da32ff4810aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454066} {:answer/id #uuid "9379cea3-738f-5b45-9ffb-a0d389c84fcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454067}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9379cea3-738f-5b45-9ffb-a0d389c84fcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454067} :answer-field/id #uuid "ecc3054a-806e-55e3-a67b-9d3aafb6ab0e" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454783} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "862f1c15-7d4f-5155-be39-3424fe47a6a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454068} {:answer/id #uuid "e30f18bc-42c2-57a7-8e53-faed108c78b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454069}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "862f1c15-7d4f-5155-be39-3424fe47a6a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454068} :answer-field/id #uuid "6338d248-c558-59d6-b0d2-c36e277fc0ef" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454784} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ff828bb-30f0-59e3-937e-d221fd6fafb8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454070} {:answer/id #uuid "5d13fad8-f3e6-549c-954e-a199b234815c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454071}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5d13fad8-f3e6-549c-954e-a199b234815c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454071} :answer-field/id #uuid "693882b2-096a-516e-95d6-0393826e4576" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454785}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "806aafe6-aa9d-53f3-a7d9-19809d388a29" :question/math-academy-id "q-82092" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** **If** $7$ is an even number, **then** $6$ is an odd number.\n- **II.** **If** $6$ is an even number, **then** $7$ is an even number.\n- **III.** **If** $6$ is an even number, **then** $7$ is an odd number." :question/worked-solution "An implication $A⇒B$ is true *unless* $A$ is true and $B$ is false. In other words, the implication is true unless the \"promise\" is broken.\n\n- Statement I is true. The antecedent \"$7$ is an even number\" is false, so the promise does not apply. Regardless of the consequent, the promise is *not* broken, and the statement is true.\n\n- Statement II is false. The antecedent \"$6$ is an even number\" is true, and the consequent \"$7$ is an even number\" is false. So the promise is broken, and the statement is false.\n\n- Statement III is true. The antecedent \"$6$ is an even number\" is true, and the consequent \"$7$ is an odd number\" is true. So the promise is kept, and the statement is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407133 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152089 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6927f03c-aa7a-56ac-8cd0-c036a11aadc9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Truth Value of a Statement Involving Nested Quantifiers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49953372-6786-55fd-b957-4551684db7d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453670} {:answer/id #uuid "eb694d2a-846a-5113-a363-79bb2236c246" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453671}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb694d2a-846a-5113-a363-79bb2236c246" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453671} :answer-field/id #uuid "75840e40-2cca-58f4-a515-e9cfdb46f959" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454585} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "57c979c3-fafa-584e-abe1-50aaafd5442e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453672} {:answer/id #uuid "374d893b-950f-54cb-a1f5-2cd335ae552b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453673}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "57c979c3-fafa-584e-abe1-50aaafd5442e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453672} :answer-field/id #uuid "726bad40-3e61-5e83-b318-93789e8c9f1e" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454586} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d9be598-49fa-52b8-a352-44784bf90317" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453674} {:answer/id #uuid "e6cb932f-f971-54a3-ad09-1463e1bb7456" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453675}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e6cb932f-f971-54a3-ad09-1463e1bb7456" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453675} :answer-field/id #uuid "9963ef57-4cea-572c-8d46-02df8158a551" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454587}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0a806540-0634-5e11-9ba2-ff988650a653" :question/math-academy-id "q-183877" :question/problem "Let $p\\in Q$ and $q\\in Q.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $∃\\,p\\in Q,\\,2p=-1.$\n- **II.** The truth set of the predicate $(\\,∃\\,p\\in Q,\\,p\\cdot q=-1\\,)$ is $Q.$\n- **III.** $∃\\,q,p\\in Q,\\,p\\cdot q=-1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the statement \n\n$$\n∃\\,q,p\\in Q,\\,p\\cdot q=-1\n$$\n\nfrom option III reads as follows:\n\n$\\,$ There exist rationals $q$ and $p,$ such that $p\\cdot q=-1.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true, $2p=-1$ for some rational number $p$ (e.g., for $p=-\\frac{1}{2}$).\n\n- Statement II is false. For the predicate\n\n$$\nP(q):\\,∃\\,p\\in Q,\\,p\\cdot q=-1\n$$\n\nwe note that $P(q)$ is true for some $q\\in Q$ and false for others. For example, \n\n$$\nP(0):\\,∃\\,p\\in Q,\\,p\\cdot 0=-1\n$$\n\nis false. However, \n\n$$\nP(1):\\,∃\\,p\\in Q,\\,p\\cdot 1=-1\n$$\n\nis true, since we can take $p=-1.$\n\n- Statement III is true. The sentence \n\n$$\n(\\,∃\\,q,p\\in Q,\\,p\\cdot q=-1\\,)\n$$\n\n \ncan be written as\n\n$$\n∃q\\in Q\\,(\\,{{∃p\\in Q,\\,p\\cdot q=-1}_{⏟}}_{P(q)}\\,)\n$$\n\nwhich is true whenever the inner predicate $P(q)$ has a nonempty truth set. And according to the discussion in statement II, this is the case.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407498 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161919 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "559e653a-2ab9-54a8-84e3-02bf106a8f47" :knowledge-point/title "Inferring Divisibility in Algebraic Expressions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "737ddb9c-20f6-56c9-b552-48af2b027a57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453812} {:answer/id #uuid "8393d104-6db5-5931-886e-bb8328757c17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 