n.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "677c3e63-2822-579f-a67a-69517e4d5770" :question/math-academy-id "q-221927" :question/problem "Which of the following statements must be true for any integers $x$ and $y?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $5∣(8x+6y)$\n- **II.** $2∣(8x+6y)$\n- **III.** $3∣(8x+6y)$" :question/worked-solution "The notation $a∣b$ means $a$ divides $b.$\n\nAccording to the definition of integer divisibility, the fact that $a$ divides $b$ means that there exists an integer $k$ such that \n\n$$\nb=ak.\n$$\n\n \nWith that in mind, let's examine our statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. For example, if $x=1$ and $y=0,$ we have $8(1)+6(0)=8,$ which is not divisible by $5.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Notice that \n\n$$\n8x+6y=2(4x+3y).\n$$\n\nSince $x$ and $y$ are integers, $4x+3y$ must be an integer, too. So, $2∣(8x+6y).$\n\n- Statement III is false. For example, if $x=1$ and $y=0,$ we have $8(1)+6(0)=8,$ which is not divisible by $3.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407500 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161919 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "559e653a-2ab9-54a8-84e3-02bf106a8f47" :knowledge-point/title "Inferring Divisibility in Algebraic Expressions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9d7aada3-3e24-5121-86ae-89299aa51b2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453824} {:answer/id #uuid "7a52737c-03fb-5761-ad9b-a5d82aac901b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453825}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9d7aada3-3e24-5121-86ae-89299aa51b2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453824} :answer-field/id #uuid "272d23c5-a5f4-5031-93eb-715e0de1331a" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454662} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ac9ed580-5abc-5cb4-b0c2-5d08de51e6cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453826} {:answer/id #uuid "decf500b-cd93-5a85-9b7e-36f56dbc71ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453827}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "decf500b-cd93-5a85-9b7e-36f56dbc71ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453827} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b4f101e-0733-5560-bd04-28d8b749a607" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454663} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "264d1777-449d-5d90-b205-7657f22710de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453828} {:answer/id #uuid "72944c17-284c-55fd-9b7b-1cb36ea197e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453829}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "264d1777-449d-5d90-b205-7657f22710de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453828} :answer-field/id #uuid "74caa1f5-58f3-54e2-b8aa-662f673f7ba6" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454664}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "87475b8f-4c6f-5041-abc0-cc4d71389ee6" :question/math-academy-id "q-221928" :question/problem "Which of the following statements must be true for any integers $x$ and $y?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $3$ divides $(8x+6y)$\n- **II.** $2$ divides $(8x+6y)$\n- **III.** $4$ divides $(8x+6y)$" :question/worked-solution "The notation $a∣b$ means $a$ divides $b.$\n\nAccording to the definition of integer divisibility, the fact that $a$ divides $b$ means that there exists an integer $k$ such that \n\n$$\nb=ak.\n$$\n\n \nWith that in mind, let's examine our statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. For example, if $x=1$ and $y=0,$ we have $8(1)+6(0)=8,$ which is not divisible by $3.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Notice that \n\n$$\n8x+6y=2(4x+3y).\n$$\n\nSince $x$ and $y$ are integers, $4x+3y$ must be an integer, too. So, $2$ divides $(8x+6y).$\n\n- Statement III is false. For example, if $x=0$ and $y=1,$ we have $8(0)+6(1)=6,$ which is not divisible by $4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407505 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161919 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "559e653a-2ab9-54a8-84e3-02bf106a8f47" :knowledge-point/title "Inferring Divisibility in Algebraic Expressions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ba33ae8-ebcb-5138-8360-8827a4086e77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453836} {:answer/id #uuid "456b6334-ff0e-5966-90f2-5c51a1ddd706" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453837}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "456b6334-ff0e-5966-90f2-5c51a1ddd706" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453837} :answer-field/id #uuid "fab1cedf-cc91-5eea-89d5-dcab0106295b" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454668} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f842d8bd-31b0-5686-bfa3-548f19e273a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453838} {:answer/id #uuid "ca1c01cf-3d68-5f93-8e43-8605005468a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453839}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca1c01cf-3d68-5f93-8e43-8605005468a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453839} :answer-field/id #uuid "2db380cf-aaea-5f16-9283-d7c95560d427" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454669} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00534dc3-4006-5bef-9575-96f837e9a134" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453840} {:answer/id #uuid "fe7abe4f-841c-5bd9-ae12-d42fe2195a96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453841}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "00534dc3-4006-5bef-9575-96f837e9a134" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453840} :answer-field/id #uuid "44a3b668-b559-550b-9651-be66b31864e6" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454670}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e7df593d-9767-5ee4-9c1c-cf41d12d4aeb" :question/math-academy-id "q-221932" :question/problem "Which of the following statements must be true for any integers $x$ and $y?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $6$ divides $(24x+30y)$\n- **II.** $3$ divides $(24x+30y)$\n- **III.** $5$ divides $(24x+30y)$" :question/worked-solution "The notation $a∣b$ means $a$ divides $b.$\n\nAccording to the definition of integer divisibility, the fact that $a$ divides $b$ means that there exists an integer $k$ such that \n\n$$\nb=ak.\n$$\n\n \nWith that in mind, let's examine our statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Notice that \n\n$$\n24x+30y=6(4x+5y).\n$$\n\nSince $x$ and $y$ are integers, $4x+5y$ must be an integer, too. So, $6$ divides $(24x+30y).$\n\n- Statement II is true. Notice that \n\n$$\n24x+30y=3(8x+10y).\n$$\n\nSince $x$ and $y$ are integers, $8x+10y$ must be an integer, too. So, $3$ divides $(24x+30y).$\n\n- Statement III is false. For example, if $x=-1$ and $y=1,$ we have $24(-1)+30(1)=6,$ which is not divisible by $5.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \" I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407778 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124485 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "486cc512-416b-5eac-8964-1a87d533de72" :knowledge-point/title "Determining if a Given Set Is Linearly Independent Given Information on Its Elements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d8c3ee6-fd37-5cb0-b0ab-80e7a7cca090" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454166} {:answer/id #uuid "cd824f2a-c47c-53a0-be26-c6bd74e52573" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454167}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd824f2a-c47c-53a0-be26-c6bd74e52573" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454167} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b613250-bfe0-5d10-933a-62b1f7c0e186" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454833} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e25a9185-5eae-580c-a0fe-a1704d681147" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454168} {:answer/id #uuid "0d8662e3-fc5d-5d99-afd6-2bc7152d04fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454169}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e25a9185-5eae-580c-a0fe-a1704d681147" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454168} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa4d6e3a-1748-5dc1-aec5-5bf919354400" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454834} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e6560a1-a8ef-5d21-8325-256e585e4826" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454170} {:answer/id #uuid "7e317d01-b088-5a71-957d-334271a2bf38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454171}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e6560a1-a8ef-5d21-8325-256e585e4826" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454170} :answer-field/id #uuid "528428ad-5f38-5fd7-92de-7aab58b61f83" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454835}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e5252a0f-1ef3-54ce-a8b5-332d495a5706" :question/math-academy-id "q-94782" :question/problem "Consider a vector space $V$ and vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}\\in V.$ Given that ${{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is a linearly independent set and ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},\\text{ }{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is a linearly dependent one, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${v}_{1}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{2}$, ${v}_{3}$ and ${v}_{4}$\n- **II.** ${v}_{2}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{3}$ and ${v}_{4}$\n- **III.** ${v}_{2}+{v}_{3}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{2}$ and ${v}_{4}$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given options in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Since ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is a linearly dependent set, we obtain that\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0\n$$\n\nhas a non-zero solution. Moreover, ${x}_{1}$ can't be zero because then\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0\n$$\n\nwill have a non-zero solution and that's a contradiction as ${{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is linearly independent.\nTherefore, from ${x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=-\\frac{{x}_{2}}{{x}_{1}}{v}_{2}-\\frac{{x}_{3}}{{x}_{1}}{v}_{3}-\\frac{{x}_{4}}{{x}_{1}}{v}_{4}.\n$$\n\nThis means that ${v}_{1}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{2}$, ${v}_{3},$ and ${v}_{4}.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since ${{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is a linearly independent set, ${v}_{2}$ can not be a linear combination of other vectors.\n\n- Statement III is false. Since ${{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is a linearly independent set, ${v}_{3}$ can not be a linear combination of ${v}_{2}$ and ${v}_{4}.$ As a result ${v}_{2}+{v}_{3}$ can't be written as combination of ${v}_{2}$ and ${v}_{4}$ too.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407814 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152083 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "320c4694-1904-5fc7-a324-a4c89f0e3257" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Involving Existential Quantifiers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33eb7a72-fa8b-50b1-8ebc-aa7cd26028d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453788} {:answer/id #uuid "3f148267-ad3c-5618-bf40-bc705ab3bdfb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453789}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "33eb7a72-fa8b-50b1-8ebc-aa7cd26028d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453788} :answer-field/id #uuid "67801945-6aa3-515f-8437-a181eaacb168" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454644} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d11772ef-6953-5831-a364-4f095ce61082" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453790} {:answer/id #uuid "cdadec83-dd68-5de6-9b35-29095538b458" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453791}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cdadec83-dd68-5de6-9b35-29095538b458" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453791} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b72408b-26ba-54eb-8d07-5b7664c2b69b" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454645} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d70677ff-f22c-5a54-9108-c31451ca7b61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453792} {:answer/id #uuid "770e6a80-ad13-537e-945d-03549ab8a101" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453793}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "770e6a80-ad13-537e-945d-03549ab8a101" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453793} :answer-field/id #uuid "f38af25e-8a36-5fa8-838f-9acec9abb00b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454646}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5404de7a-e750-5076-ba3f-b3642f799e6f" :question/math-academy-id "q-216495" :question/problem "$\\,$ $P(n):$ $n$ is odd or $n+1$ is odd\n\nGiven that the above predicate is defined over the universal set $N,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The truth set of $P(n)$ is $∅.$\n- **II.** The truth set of $P(n)$ is $N.$\n- **III.** $∃n\\in N,\\,P(n).$" :question/worked-solution "The *existential quantification* of a predicate $P(x),$ defined over the universal set $U,$ transforms this predicate into a statement that we write as\n\n$$\n∃x\\in U,\\,P(x).\n$$\n\nThis statement is true if the predicate $P(x)$ is true for a single element $x\\in U,$ i.e. if the truth set ${T}_{P}$ of the predicate is not empty:\n\n$$\n{T}_{P}\\ne ∅\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that:\n\n- the truth set of \"$n$ is odd\" is the set of odd natural numbers, and\n\n- the truth set of \"$n+1$ is odd\" is the set of even natural numbers.\n\nSo, the truth set of our predicate is\n\n$$\n{T}_{P}={\\text{odd natural numbers}}\\cup {\\text{even natural numbers}}=N.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. The truth set is *not* empty.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, ${T}_{P}=N.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since ${T}_{P}$ is *not* empty, the statement $∃n\\in N,\\,P(n)$ is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407847 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124457 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "29610715-333d-5e0c-9328-eec1d45f56ed" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Limits Along Different Paths for Multivariable Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08c4d527-5e01-5264-8001-c16ba5c829f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453880} {:answer/id #uuid "8a788be2-6daa-5a9a-b61f-b090c8b8cf80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453881}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8a788be2-6daa-5a9a-b61f-b090c8b8cf80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453881} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d46ebdc-4ea8-5b5d-a791-12ebf82b2b2b" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454690} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e7662fdd-d050-5004-a857-2d86c30b4a05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453882} {:answer/id #uuid "9233290a-d139-5d2d-91b5-3115178cf2c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453883}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e7662fdd-d050-5004-a857-2d86c30b4a05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453882} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e9a1015-1583-5e39-b729-2685f362e667" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454691} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25f5a5f0-e3d5-58cb-a9a2-e0e244128177" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453884} {:answer/id #uuid "6013b3d6-d8f8-5f12-8351-83ccb30ce208" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453885}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25f5a5f0-e3d5-58cb-a9a2-e0e244128177" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453884} :answer-field/id #uuid "81040326-5134-5a42-8539-aac88ecd9a5e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454692}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a9a907de-0404-5ffb-8362-e9676298070b" :question/math-academy-id "q-36139" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the limit given below?\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+2y}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The limit evaluates to $\\frac{1}{3}$ along the path $y={x}^{2}$\n- **II.** The limit evaluates to $-1$ along the path $y=-{x}^{2}$\n- **III.** The limit exists and is equal to $\\frac{1}{3}$" :question/worked-solution "Attempting to evaluate the limit by direct substitution leads to the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0}:$\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+2y}=\\frac{0}{{0}^{2}+2\\cdot 0}=\\frac{0}{0}\n$$\n\nHowever, the function cannot be simplified by canceling common factors in the numerator and denominator:\n\nWe attempt to evaluate the limit by approaching $(0,0)$ from different paths.\n\n- Statement I is true. Taking $x\\to (0,0)$ along the path $y={x}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)\\,\\,\\,y={x}^{2}}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+2y} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+2{x}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3{x}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Taking $x\\to (0,0)$ along the path $y=-{x}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)\\,\\,\\,y=-{x}^{2}}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+2y} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{-{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+2(-{x}^{2})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{-{x}^{2}}{-{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Because the limit evaluates to different results on two different paths, we conclude that the limit does not exist:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+2y}=\\text{DNE}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407886 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152197 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "99c2db8c-670b-521b-8942-3b89f1e95d3f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Injections For Functions Whose Domain or Codomain Are Real Intervals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e09de5d-566b-53b7-938e-4cd69784f908" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453162} {:answer/id #uuid "09739bfe-5ef1-5a91-a5aa-5281c92dda9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453163}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e09de5d-566b-53b7-938e-4cd69784f908" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453162} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6d5a350-84ff-5946-86f2-1d19d8d7220c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454331} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8cee3daa-3190-55b4-a76d-c60b5757491d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453164} {:answer/id #uuid "f84f942c-6e9f-5b7c-af7b-f2c81298fce5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453165}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f84f942c-6e9f-5b7c-af7b-f2c81298fce5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453165} :answer-field/id #uuid "631b3c6b-1149-5d42-a891-5e829966c88f" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454332} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "53fda273-36a0-5e47-98ef-2cc2874bb65a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453166} {:answer/id #uuid "747834de-2a79-5887-b0c3-1e01bf258a61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453167}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "747834de-2a79-5887-b0c3-1e01bf258a61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453167} :answer-field/id #uuid "cae9ece0-8770-5aea-a183-8518985dc8d5" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454333}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1a3dbd42-cd16-5083-8842-33f0028feb3d" :question/math-academy-id "q-105207" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:[-2,4]\\to [-3,9]$ which is given by $f(x)=2x+1?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $f(-2)=f(4)$\n- **II.** $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in [-2,4],$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$\n- **III.** $f$ is an injection" :question/worked-solution "First, we graph the function.\n\n![](images/5f/5fd931a87d6a5fb32d10ed931f443a8175f0760eba9fe2fe69336f8f79e9fd68.png)\n\nA function $f:X\\to Y$ is an injection (also known as *one-to-one*) if *every* element in $X$ is mapped to a *distinct* element in $Y:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. We have $f(2)=2(-2)+1=-3$ and $f(4)=2\\cdot 4+1=9.$\n\n- Statement II is true. As we can see from the graph, it passes the horizontal line test, meaning that there are no two distinct elements within $[-2,4]$ that map to the same element in $[-3,9].$ So, for all ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ contained within the domain $[-2,4],$ if $f({x}_{1})$ and $f({x}_{2})$ are equal, then we must have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, since statement II is true, $f$ is an injection.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408038 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192801 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "441a1de0-dc64-59fe-99a8-0ab502841425" :knowledge-point/title "Checking Whether a Given Function Is a Valid PDF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "abd3b4ad-7245-5359-aa08-f555f6155e8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453466} {:answer/id #uuid "cdfa7c36-5307-50a0-bf63-41b72cb111a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453467}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cdfa7c36-5307-50a0-bf63-41b72cb111a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453467} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ace91eb-339b-5d50-a799-7b88dbafe125" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454483} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d15f02a2-e02d-5286-a449-4115be4fc330" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453468} {:answer/id #uuid "81e8d8a3-4012-5902-b1fd-cd50cc9744af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453469}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81e8d8a3-4012-5902-b1fd-cd50cc9744af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453469} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f2197b0-eada-5d24-bd2b-fe0d8b2c6994" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454484} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "305dbab8-5c7a-5858-b8d4-92e8c2368110" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453470} {:answer/id #uuid "ab13c02c-2738-5b13-ae31-2638c7d3c679" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453471}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab13c02c-2738-5b13-ae31-2638c7d3c679" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453471} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4c2b331-d72c-5f5c-8d12-1798339f28ae" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454485}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b46ac655-a97e-50cb-a022-2af841ed15e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-160451" :question/problem "$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{{x}^{8}},\\, & x\\ge 1, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven the function $f(x)$ above, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\ge 1$\n- **II.** ${\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n- **III.** $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a valid probability density function on a set $S,$ it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nNow, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, for $x\\ge 1,$ we have $f(x)=\\frac{7}{{x}^{8}}\\ge 0.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{7}{{x}^{8}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{7}}\\,{|}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =-(0-1) \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statements I and II are true, the first and second conditions are satisfied. So, $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409434 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152073 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "398716c2-d0e6-5106-a702-2f71d957726f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Congruent Integers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d490cf1-d662-56a2-8631-21d543f11c23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453120} {:answer/id #uuid "ce480cda-9021-5f06-a8cd-b9ca16301c27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453121}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3d490cf1-d662-56a2-8631-21d543f11c23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453120} :answer-field/id #uuid "af1230fc-88f6-56f0-a44f-a2580bb43a87" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454310} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f5f14a7e-4460-5c56-88cd-b67e7eb770b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453122} {:answer/id #uuid "168ce81c-a8ca-550c-ae67-a01761495d2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453123}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f5f14a7e-4460-5c56-88cd-b67e7eb770b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453122} :answer-field/id #uuid "89b1c902-2a3c-5a5a-8275-9ced53169a21" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454311} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9917c881-2ee9-5be2-b248-f90217ecd423" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453124} {:answer/id #uuid "f8a8e630-8f3b-5355-ac11-368a8e967b4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453125}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8a8e630-8f3b-5355-ac11-368a8e967b4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453125} :answer-field/id #uuid "0490fa62-dcfa-5271-a176-054c103e687c" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454312}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2a4a4ae5-eba9-597a-b12c-2ce503fbc86a" :question/math-academy-id "q-103385" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $11≡3\\,(\\text{mod}\\,3)$\n- **II.** $18≡16\\,(\\text{mod}\\,4)$\n- **III.** $24≡19\\,(\\text{mod}\\,5)$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall that \n\n$$\na≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,n∣(a-b).\n$$\n\nSo, $a$ and $b$ are congruent modulo $n$ if and only if $(a-b)$ is divisible by $n$ (there is no remainder).\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Case I gives a false statement because $3∤(11-3).$ Notice that $11-3=8,$ which is not divisible by $3.$\n\n- Case II gives a false statement because $4∤(18-16).$ Notice that $18-16=2,$ which is not divisible by $4.$\n\n- Case III gives a true statement. Indeed, $5∣(24-19).$ There is no remainder:\n\n$$\n(24-19)÷5=5÷5=1\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409435 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152074 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2eebe007-8a95-578d-b553-e37a7bd8a327" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Congruent Negative Integers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f6939e2c-5e4c-5d3c-b411-121e989019d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453964} {:answer/id #uuid "42527d1d-51eb-5aa0-b849-c3505c852646" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453965}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f6939e2c-5e4c-5d3c-b411-121e989019d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453964} :answer-field/id #uuid "c65be09a-f53c-5c58-909a-d975c0b29817" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454732} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dbaf0ed3-4c76-557d-bc51-6406555d6dc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453966} {:answer/id #uuid "c93051af-e99c-5c12-a773-dfc66b74d11a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453967}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dbaf0ed3-4c76-557d-bc51-6406555d6dc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453966} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8d44745-35ed-5099-bb46-c9a6bdbcf88a" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454733} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e654702c-0d8c-5636-9f91-64969cdd47b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453968} {:answer/id #uuid "e6d41efc-3f6b-5285-a299-04b9702a043c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453969}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e6d41efc-3f6b-5285-a299-04b9702a043c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453969} :answer-field/id #uuid "7387b7e6-f6df-542e-b959-1cad4caa776a" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454734}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "42227076-6750-5c0c-9261-152604f91699" :question/math-academy-id "q-76953" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $17≡2\\,(\\text{mod}\\,9)$\n- **II.** $23≡-10\\,(\\text{mod}\\,5)$\n- **III.** $33≡12\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7)$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall that \n\n$$\na≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,n∣(a-b).\n$$\n\nSo, $a$ and $b$ are congruent modulo $n$ if and only if $(a-b)$ is divisible by $n$ (there is no remainder).\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false because $9∤(17-2).$ Notice that $17-2=15,$ which is not divisible by $9.$\n\n- Statement II is false because $5∤(23-(-10)).$ Notice that $23-(-10)=33,$ which is not divisible by $5.$\n\n- Statement III is true because $7\\,|\\,(33-12).$ There is no remainder:\n\n$$\n(33-12)÷7=21÷7=3\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409440 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152074 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2eebe007-8a95-578d-b553-e37a7bd8a327" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Congruent Negative Integers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2325c00a-6377-5d3f-8e31-1a81805e5899" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453970} {:answer/id #uuid "8c6dd81c-8cb5-59f5-a508-2111c88efa9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453971}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c6dd81c-8cb5-59f5-a508-2111c88efa9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453971} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b371275-6d7b-5b97-8c3b-4bd36ec051e3" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454735} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a2d67da-1615-5493-bc76-35012297de9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453972} {:answer/id #uuid "18ef6a60-8030-55f2-9da0-921283250a88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453973}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a2d67da-1615-5493-bc76-35012297de9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453972} :answer-field/id #uuid "6252a9b3-c085-5ff6-bf8e-08227b893b43" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454736} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c1e360a-6eaa-5672-b5fd-0ff6e047a87c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453974} {:answer/id #uuid "41922cf8-75b9-562c-8d22-97b501963686" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453975}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "41922cf8-75b9-562c-8d22-97b501963686" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453975} :answer-field/id #uuid "3486679b-149d-5c68-b66e-923ed8ccc572" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454737}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ae89ee49-3f2d-51e4-a2f6-ac3e918a674e" :question/math-academy-id "q-76958" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $12≡36\\,(\\text{mod}\\,2)$\n- **II.** $-9≡18\\,(\\text{mod}\\,4)$\n- **III.** $21≡45\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8)$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall that \n\n$$\na≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,n∣(a-b).\n$$\n\nSo, $a$ and $b$ are congruent modulo $n$ if and only if $(a-b)$ is divisible by $n$ (there is no remainder).\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true because $2∣(12-36).$ There is no remainder:\n\n$$\n(12-36)÷2=-24÷2=-12\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false because $4∤(-9-18).$ Notice that $-9-18=-27,$ which is not divisible by $4.$\n\n- Statement III is true because $8\\,|\\,(21-45).$ There is no remainder:\n\n$$\n(21-45)÷8=-24÷8=-3\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409441 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152074 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2eebe007-8a95-578d-b553-e37a7bd8a327" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Congruent Negative Integers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f096c075-5b46-5ce6-a234-377c581a476b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453976} {:answer/id #uuid "6863ca49-960a-5d77-9a3a-7d0d0aa1dd85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453977}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f096c075-5b46-5ce6-a234-377c581a476b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453976} :answer-field/id #uuid "e94e7c51-516a-5014-af78-5555d5511fb7" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454738} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dc0ffaae-5eca-57b7-a644-173f07d6b749" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453978} {:answer/id #uuid "e0e3cde8-deea-59b4-8676-00eeb50e5aff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453979}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e0e3cde8-deea-59b4-8676-00eeb50e5aff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453979} :answer-field/id #uuid "9cdc0adf-283c-5e72-a33c-9caf5b09e916" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454739} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a4664ac9-65c6-53be-af21-37ab3cf61812" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453980} {:answer/id #uuid "b5e95427-5a86-5e7d-9c59-7539f2ab125f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453981}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a4664ac9-65c6-53be-af21-37ab3cf61812" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453980} :answer-field/id #uuid "4cb6cfb2-0eb7-58cd-885c-671d59601b18" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454740}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b17c24c5-e750-5126-8785-6318018ca783" :question/math-academy-id "q-76959" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $-5≡11\\,(\\text{mod}\\,3)$\n- **II.** $-7≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7)$\n- **III.** $6≡25\\,(\\text{mod}\\,9)$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall that \n\n$$\na≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,n∣(a-b).\n$$\n\nSo, $a$ and $b$ are congruent modulo $n$ if and only if $(a-b)$ is divisible by $n$ (there is no remainder).\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false because $3∤(-5-11).$ Notice that $-5-11=-16,$ which is not divisible by $3.$\n\n- Statement II is true because $7\\,|\\,(-7-0).$ There is no remainder:\n\n$$\n(-7-0)÷7=-7÷7=-7\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false because $9∤(6-25).$ Notice that $6-25=-19,$ which is not divisible by $9.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409482 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152223 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e2cb28a0-b456-55cc-94c3-2a35edde21be" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Integers are Coprime"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16764622-cd26-55e1-8a5a-7e55b57682c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454286} {:answer/id #uuid "ba98f67b-67c0-5060-a532-9100f74d628f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 1