592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9e2b9768-6303-5aa7-8a02-db48065ae94a" :question/math-academy-id "q-98476" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\text{gcd}(5719,2669)=1$\n- **II.** $\\text{gcd}(5719,2669)=3$\n- **III.** $5719$ and $2669$ are coprime" :question/worked-solution "Recall that two integers are coprime if their greatest common divisor is $1.$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true, while statement II is false. Indeed, let's use the Euclidean algorithm, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}5719 & = & 2669\\cdot 2 & + & 381 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 2669 & = & 381\\cdot 7 & + & 2 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 381 & = & 2\\cdot 190 & + & 1 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 2 & = & 1\\cdot 2 & + & 0\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe last positive remainder is $1.$ So, the greatest common divisor of $5719$ and $2669$ is $1:$\n\n$$\n\\text{gcd}(5719,2669)=1.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $\\text{gcd}(5719,2669)=1,$ the numbers are coprime.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409557 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124466 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9d090462-a031-5f96-ac13-90dac882edab" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Points Where Partial Derivatives Exist"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e148fac7-727b-55d9-ba67-0a9fc7a276e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453368} {:answer/id #uuid "6c6ec723-5cd2-5173-b8f1-1778f583295d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453369}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6c6ec723-5cd2-5173-b8f1-1778f583295d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453369} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e8e1392-18d1-56b3-b0f5-ff3dd861687a" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454434} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a536093-cb71-5d44-a52f-8e05b4b9f74a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453370} {:answer/id #uuid "cc2d5ab2-a228-5241-aef5-decbffea282c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453371}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc2d5ab2-a228-5241-aef5-decbffea282c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453371} :answer-field/id #uuid "deacc4af-75f1-5a94-a0d0-5d1ad4ac3ea8" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454435} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80b4f556-0cc0-5fc7-9fac-56ff9260d6c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453372} {:answer/id #uuid "cbd91732-9818-5742-9c5d-ea668d6dbe0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453373}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cbd91732-9818-5742-9c5d-ea668d6dbe0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453373} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f7af479-38a3-58de-bca6-c137a88e2790" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454436}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0a3b6388-98bd-5083-8d1c-f60a05890b23" :question/math-academy-id "q-132726" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true about the function $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{y})?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** Both partial derivatives exist at the point $(\\sqrt{3},1)$\n- **II.** ${f}_{x}(1,\\sqrt{3})$ is defined\n- **III.** ${f}_{y}(0,1)$ is defined" :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the partial derivatives of $f(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{(\\frac{x}{y})}^{2}+1}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{x}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}}+1}\\cdot \\frac{1}{y} \\\\  & =\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{y} \\\\  & =\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{(\\frac{x}{y})}^{2}+1}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{x}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}}+1}\\cdot (-\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\cdot (-\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's examine the statements one-by-one.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, the function $f$ is defined at $(\\sqrt{3},1)$, where we have \n\n$$\nf(\\sqrt{3},1)=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{1})=\\frac{\\pi }{3},\n$$\n\nand both partial derivatives are also defined at $(\\sqrt{3},1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(\\sqrt{3},1) & =\\frac{1}{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}+{1}^{2}}=\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ {f}_{y}(\\sqrt{3},1) & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}+{1}^{2}}=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, the function $f$ itself is defined at $(1,\\sqrt{3})$, where we have \n\n$$\nf(1,\\sqrt{3})=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}})=\\frac{\\pi }{6},\n$$\n\nand ${f}_{x}$ is also defined at $(1,\\sqrt{3}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(1,\\sqrt{3})=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{{1}^{2}+(\\sqrt{3})^{2}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is also true. Indeed, the function $f$ itself is defined at $(0,1)$, where we have \n\n$$\nf(0,1)=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{0}{1})=0,\n$$\n\nand ${f}_{y}$ is also defined at $(0,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(0,1)=-\\frac{0}{{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409558 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124466 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9d090462-a031-5f96-ac13-90dac882edab" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Points Where Partial Derivatives Exist"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "899f43e4-fc9a-5506-b84d-a25c2d9eb6f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453928} {:answer/id #uuid "ec4690b4-12f7-5ffd-a0f0-d137fa95703c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453929}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "899f43e4-fc9a-5506-b84d-a25c2d9eb6f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453928} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ccf0ae7-dc64-51f0-892e-8d88c6910e82" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454714} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "376cf739-f8d8-5cb0-91a0-52b41ea250c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453930} {:answer/id #uuid "ffcc07c3-7704-591c-aebf-ff0249e9dd10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453931}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ffcc07c3-7704-591c-aebf-ff0249e9dd10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453931} :answer-field/id #uuid "72f29120-e8c2-52fc-abd7-8386d5f878c4" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454715} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fc77c615-3280-58d4-a19d-18282a3f7486" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453932} {:answer/id #uuid "8cfc9ce4-4706-5c6b-8f71-059b43d404d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453933}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fc77c615-3280-58d4-a19d-18282a3f7486" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453932} :answer-field/id #uuid "a7c89136-ff34-5898-9f58-5a98f17bcfb1" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454716}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "538fdcf0-8dcd-525c-becd-0317742dbf1a" :question/math-academy-id "q-72010" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true about the function $f(x,y)={e}^{\\sqrt{xy}}?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** Both partial derivatives exist at the point $(1,-1)$\n\n- **II.** ${f}_{y}(-1,-1)$ is defined\n\n- **III.** ${f}_{x}(0,1)$ is defined" :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the partial derivatives of $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & ={e}^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\cdot \\frac{y}{2\\sqrt{xy}} \\\\  & =\\frac{y{e}^{\\sqrt{xy}}}{2\\sqrt{xy}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & ={e}^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\cdot \\frac{x}{2\\sqrt{xy}} \\\\  & =\\frac{x{e}^{\\sqrt{xy}}}{2\\sqrt{xy}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's examine the statements one-by-one. \n\n- Statement I is false. If we substitute $(1,-1)$ into $f$, we get\n\n$$\nf(1,-1)={e}^{\\sqrt{(1)(-1)}}=-{e}^{\\sqrt{-1}}\n$$\n\nwhich is undefined since we have a negative number under the radical.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, the function $f$ is defined at $(-1,-1)$, where we have \n\n$$\nf(-1,-1)={e}^{\\sqrt{(-1)(-1)}}={e}^{\\sqrt{1}}={e}^{1}=e,\n$$\n\nand ${f}_{y}$ is also defined at $(-1,-1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(-1,-1) & =\\frac{(-1){e}^{\\sqrt{(-1)(-1)}}}{2\\sqrt{(-1)(-1)}}=-\\frac{{e}^{\\sqrt{1}}}{2\\sqrt{1}}=-\\frac{e}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. If we substitute $(0,1)$ into ${f}_{x}$, we get\n\n$$\n{f}_{x}(0,1)=1\\cdot \\frac{{e}^{\\sqrt{0\\cdot 1}}}{2\\sqrt{0\\cdot 1}}=\\frac{{e}^{0}}{2\\sqrt{0}}=\\frac{1}{0},\n$$\n\nwhich is undefined since we have division by zero.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is 'II  only'."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409584 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059689 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0d56b033-a2c8-57c7-adde-e574d726ec78" :knowledge-point/title "Rewriting Symbolic Conditional Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6d0f8fb4-d1b2-5bff-ba27-c6e4e679e31c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453634} {:answer/id #uuid "8e7d44c8-3ad6-50d2-9658-d18a60e921c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453635}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e7d44c8-3ad6-50d2-9658-d18a60e921c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453635} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ba7a927-c65d-53d2-a68e-2a711452828e" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454567} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d8c84692-3840-51b5-880d-3386d31c4f51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453636} {:answer/id #uuid "8dc1d84f-0a08-51e1-9122-944928bd54c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453637}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8dc1d84f-0a08-51e1-9122-944928bd54c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453637} :answer-field/id #uuid "91aa8150-4bc8-561c-9c32-8cfddb99b464" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454568} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f8ce0ad-e15d-5071-aae6-6ebf6f10905b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453638} {:answer/id #uuid "34bd4c0a-6891-5927-8f43-1900cd830078" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453639}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4f8ce0ad-e15d-5071-aae6-6ebf6f10905b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453638} :answer-field/id #uuid "728d40e4-2d8b-5727-be86-396f6263ab1f" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454569}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1308109d-5efe-51ad-bfa1-4050522344dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-182506" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A⇒¬B≡¬(A∧B)$\n- **II.** $¬(A⇒¬B)≡A∧B$\n- **III.** $¬(A⇒¬B)≡¬A∧B$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of our statements:\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, $A⇒¬B$ is logically equivalent to the disjunction $¬A∨¬B,$ which by De Morgan's law is equivalent to $¬(A∧B).$\n\n- Statement II is true, while statement III is false. From part I, we have the following equivalence:\n\n$$\nA⇒¬B≡¬(A∧B)\n$$\n\nBy negating this statement, we get\n\n$$\n¬(A⇒¬B)≡¬(¬(A∧B)).\n$$\n\nCanceling out double negation, we reach\n\n$$\nA∧B.\n$$\n\nSo, $¬(A⇒¬B)$ is equivalent to $A∧B.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409888 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092339 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd399539-33cf-5738-b970-fcc6c1d919c8" :knowledge-point/title "Using Properties of Indicator Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "73398205-b447-5295-a67c-ad006a848004" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453574} {:answer/id #uuid "66ac170a-d95d-5009-aef4-e8e0a5826587" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453575}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "66ac170a-d95d-5009-aef4-e8e0a5826587" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453575} :answer-field/id #uuid "cabc922e-c483-5964-999a-afcbcd1b58ba" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454537} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10ebd81b-61aa-58e2-8fe6-1acf2a46536f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453576} {:answer/id #uuid "c16f5c20-ce58-58cc-a4b2-847c9c364e63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453577}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "10ebd81b-61aa-58e2-8fe6-1acf2a46536f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453576} :answer-field/id #uuid "0188fa47-67f0-516d-a06e-0f6db7d50605" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454538} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31b9dc1f-cc8d-5093-ba46-67a90d725c4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453578} {:answer/id #uuid "986b4a97-0064-5e3c-bb93-d96d0717fad2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453579}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "986b4a97-0064-5e3c-bb93-d96d0717fad2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453579} :answer-field/id #uuid "1683ca8d-d357-5b5b-a758-4c8420293a37" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454539}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "09ca95e9-e7fd-5d14-80c3-ab64bc50a23d" :question/math-academy-id "q-174385" :question/problem "Given that ${1}_{A}(q)=0,$ which of the following statements about $\\overset{―}{A}$ are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${1}_{\\overset{―}{A}}\\,(q)=1$\n\n- **II.** ${1}_{\\overset{―}{A}}\\,(q)=0$\n\n- **III.** $q\\in \\overset{―}{A}$\n\n*Hint: ${1}_{A}$ denotes the indicator function of the set $A$ and ${1}_{\\overset{―}{A}}$ denotes the indicator function of the complement of $A.$*" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the indicator functions of $\\overset{―}{A},$ $A\\cap B,$ and $A\\cup B$ have the following properties:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{1}_{\\overset{―}{A}}\\,(x) & =1-{1}_{A}(x) \\\\ {1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(x) & =min\\{{1}_{A}(x),{1}_{B}(x)\\} \\\\ {1}_{A\\,\\cup \\,B}\\,(x) & =max\\{{1}_{A}(x),{1}_{B}(x)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true while statement II is false. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{1}_{\\overset{―}{A}}\\,(q) & =1-{1}_{A}(q) \\\\  & =1-0 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since ${1}_{\\overset{―}{A}}\\,(q)=1,$ we conclude that $q$ belongs to $\\overset{―}{A}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409890 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092339 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd399539-33cf-5738-b970-fcc6c1d919c8" :knowledge-point/title "Using Properties of Indicator Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9166a2cd-e482-5ef6-8dd0-7069988d19be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453592} {:answer/id #uuid "b1393175-0d07-53d3-844c-d6ae5f6863e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453593}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b1393175-0d07-53d3-844c-d6ae5f6863e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453593} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef2fa57c-2909-5935-8d3c-0c6741e819f1" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454546} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d018f001-d7c1-5d5f-ad00-a185cb6d375f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453594} {:answer/id #uuid "46f21955-ef1a-5e2c-8cda-63a6ce3b6b56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453595}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d018f001-d7c1-5d5f-ad00-a185cb6d375f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453594} :answer-field/id #uuid "459b35ad-69a1-5c21-8aec-11bb813a98f2" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454547} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8f942421-ed53-502c-8912-7b5ca533e6d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453596} {:answer/id #uuid "eb24302b-1253-5c54-afa0-b4ff91533d39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453597}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb24302b-1253-5c54-afa0-b4ff91533d39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453597} :answer-field/id #uuid "4231e57f-0807-5822-9404-6d3a419c5c18" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454548}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6c60efa7-9f70-50c9-8725-0334784ed791" :question/math-academy-id "q-174402" :question/problem "$$\n{1}_{A}(t)=1,\\,{1}_{B}(t)=1\n$$\n\nGiven the values of the indicator functions of the sets $A$ and $B,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${1}_{A\\,\\cup \\,B}\\,(t)=1$\n\n- **II.** ${1}_{A\\,\\cup \\,B}\\,(t)=0$\n\n- **III.** $t\\in A\\cup B$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the indicator functions of $\\overset{―}{A},$ $A\\cap B,$ and $A\\cup B$ have the following properties:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{1}_{\\overset{―}{A}}\\,(x) & =1-{1}_{A}(x) \\\\ {1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(x) & =min\\{{1}_{A}(x),{1}_{B}(x)\\} \\\\ {1}_{A\\,\\cup \\,B}\\,(x) & =max\\{{1}_{A}(x),{1}_{B}(x)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true while statement II is false. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{1}_{A\\,\\cup \\,B}\\,(t) & =max\\{{1}_{A}(t),{1}_{B}(t)\\} \\\\  & =max\\{1,1\\} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since ${1}_{A\\,\\cup \\,B}\\,(t)=1,$ we conclude that $t$ belongs to $A\\cup B.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409891 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092339 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd399539-33cf-5738-b970-fcc6c1d919c8" :knowledge-point/title "Using Properties of Indicator Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b4cfbc8-2b8c-5140-a8bb-7f6216d1c21a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453586} {:answer/id #uuid "07d45975-75ad-5ac0-80a2-a67332372a61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453587}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "07d45975-75ad-5ac0-80a2-a67332372a61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453587} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f5ce266-0ba2-521f-8f38-84d3b53bb633" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454543} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aa7035d2-94ee-5d7e-baff-b2c5f0b47416" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453588} {:answer/id #uuid "895992ac-82c6-5750-b799-5234f11d0dbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453589}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa7035d2-94ee-5d7e-baff-b2c5f0b47416" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453588} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b53eb93-6623-55ce-83f0-193479b58d99" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454544} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a494fefa-d26c-53e8-af8a-a80ac83e1e18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453590} {:answer/id #uuid "d42dfa9a-5b0a-598e-8bbc-e5091eaeb0f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453591}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d42dfa9a-5b0a-598e-8bbc-e5091eaeb0f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453591} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c89c5b6-f3d8-532d-9821-eeff63e9eb5a" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454545}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "92b8a61e-f7a9-5e1e-adba-90e2fa6c6243" :question/math-academy-id "q-174394" :question/problem "$$\n{1}_{A}(-1)=1,\\,{1}_{B}(-1)=1\n$$\n\nGiven the values of the indicator functions of the sets $A$ and $B,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(-1)=1$\n\n- **II.** ${1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(-1)=0$\n\n- **III.** $-1\\in A\\cap B$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the indicator functions of $\\overset{―}{A},$ $A\\cap B,$ and $A\\cup B$ have the following properties:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{1}_{\\overset{―}{A}}\\,(x) & =1-{1}_{A}(x) \\\\ {1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(x) & =min\\{{1}_{A}(x),{1}_{B}(x)\\} \\\\ {1}_{A\\,\\cup \\,B}\\,(x) & =max\\{{1}_{A}(x),{1}_{B}(x)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true while statement II is false. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(-1) & =min\\{{1}_{A}(-1),{1}_{B}(-1)\\} \\\\  & =min\\{1,1\\} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since ${1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(-1)=1,$ we conclude that $-1$ belongs to $A\\cap B.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409893 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092339 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd399539-33cf-5738-b970-fcc6c1d919c8" :knowledge-point/title "Using Properties of Indicator Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "271bd1b2-64d9-5cc7-bbec-b86ba10fc804" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453568} {:answer/id #uuid "dae1f367-953f-5742-b452-749306fe9d44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453569}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dae1f367-953f-5742-b452-749306fe9d44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453569} :answer-field/id #uuid "95b271cf-9516-5e1c-8b28-1c9dbd8c9f68" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454534} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05d4e5d4-6830-560c-878d-348a97dfcf1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453570} {:answer/id #uuid "3d8118bf-d1fb-552a-a385-b0e89891b90a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453571}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "05d4e5d4-6830-560c-878d-348a97dfcf1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453570} :answer-field/id #uuid "0189df02-b3e6-5072-80bc-52efb3c878fc" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454535} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9329cfe9-e21e-5113-b79d-99313f7bb970" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453572} {:answer/id #uuid "d680e758-2e50-5500-9ac7-2a9c9e252fa0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453573}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d680e758-2e50-5500-9ac7-2a9c9e252fa0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453573} :answer-field/id #uuid "6302a2ae-7699-51e6-afdc-d665c6513e54" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454536}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a8a05322-998a-5d01-8b89-68a8bc93dd0f" :question/math-academy-id "q-174380" :question/problem "Given that ${1}_{A}(0)=0,$ which of the following statements about $\\overset{―}{A}$ are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${1}_{\\overset{―}{A}}\\,(0)=1$\n\n- **II.** ${1}_{\\overset{―}{A}}\\,(0)=0$\n\n- **III.** $0\\in \\overset{―}{A}$\n\n*Hint: ${1}_{A}$ denotes the indicator function of the set $A$ and ${1}_{\\overset{―}{A}}$ denotes the indicator function of the complement of $A.$*" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the indicator functions of $\\overset{―}{A},$ $A\\cap B,$ and $A\\cup B$ have the following properties:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{1}_{\\overset{―}{A}}\\,(x) & =1-{1}_{A}(x) \\\\ {1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(x) & =min\\{{1}_{A}(x),{1}_{B}(x)\\} \\\\ {1}_{A\\,\\cup \\,B}\\,(x) & =max\\{{1}_{A}(x),{1}_{B}(x)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true while statement II is false. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{1}_{\\overset{―}{A}}\\,(0) & =1-{1}_{A}(0) \\\\  & =1-0 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since ${1}_{\\overset{―}{A}}\\,(0)=1,$ we conclude that $0$ belongs to $\\overset{―}{A}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410006 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161921 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "01ad9700-5aaa-5b00-8d2f-acce6ed59c9a" :knowledge-point/title "Functions Whose Codomain Is the Set of Real Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ccbbfd1c-6a08-5dc0-ae78-4e44e801c525" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454084} {:answer/id #uuid "4a04030c-b721-5bf3-be03-2ecb5763411f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454085}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ccbbfd1c-6a08-5dc0-ae78-4e44e801c525" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454084} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ef9254a-d85b-51ec-9bb3-1270c8e3b239" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454792} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a872d88-d4b7-519b-807e-1141297b7849" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454086} {:answer/id #uuid "cdd8f61b-4e41-5b3f-9d99-08b8822233ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454087}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cdd8f61b-4e41-5b3f-9d99-08b8822233ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454087} :answer-field/id #uuid "accd4fd1-1699-5f0d-895e-42caceb1cf69" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454793} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "300e70b0-e346-5a85-b265-dcd48829a1f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454088} {:answer/id #uuid "a0e966b5-2ff2-5233-acc6-ce4cf8c0ff68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454089}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a0e966b5-2ff2-5233-acc6-ce4cf8c0ff68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454089} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a2a2f00-559b-589b-b61f-d44d5d05df46" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454794}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0a60aead-59e2-5a19-8c88-b84da12bb8f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-90823" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:R\\to R$ which is given by $f(x)=2-{x}^{2}?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The range of $f$ is $(-\\infty ,-2]$\n\n- **II.** $∀\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,2],$ $∃\\,x\\in R$ such that $f(x)=y$\n\n- **III.** $f$ maps $R$ **into** $R$" :question/worked-solution "First, we graph the function.\n\n![](images/35/3575afe4fd4e5aa6754496154986b272a43fb5c035ec8d69621d52fad16ee1ea.png)\n\nRecall that $f:X\\to Y$ is an *into* function if it is not a surjection. In other words, there exists an element $y$ in $Y$ such that it has no preimage in $X:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is an into function if $∃\\,y\\in Y$ such that $∀\\,x\\in X,$ we have $f(x)\\ne y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. From the graph, the highest $y$-value is $2,$ and it occurs at the point $(0,2).$ The graph will cover all $y$-values lower than $y=2$, including $y=2$ itself. So the range of the function is $(-\\infty ,2].$\n\n- Statement II is true. Since the range of the function is $(-\\infty ,2]$, then for all $y$ contained within $(-\\infty ,2],$ there exists some $x$ contained within $R$ such that $f(x)=y.$\n\n- Statement III is true. As we can see from the range, there is no real number $x$ such that $f(x)=3\\in R.$ So, $f$ maps $R$ *into* $R.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410009 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161921 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "01ad9700-5aaa-5b00-8d2f-acce6ed59c9a" :knowledge-point/title "Functions Whose Codomain Is the Set of Real Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "015d78ce-10e6-5aa2-8e40-5fcea0882254" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453168} {:answer/id #uuid "00556d4d-0185-5264-9f2a-aa2a6f260ef6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453169}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "015d78ce-10e6-5aa2-8e40-5fcea0882254" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453168} :answer-field/id #uuid "d74da5de-c05b-5fd4-ab1e-e42243e3aba7" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454334} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e0f6634-264d-54c2-8e61-ed2f2e5776a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453170} {:answer/id #uuid "daa3ffd2-014c-5bfb-8d81-f8a7e9466f48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453171}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1e0f6634-264d-54c2-8e61-ed2f2e5776a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453170} :answer-field/id #uuid "83459419-3597-52d7-9759-0b3f9e59c3aa" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454335} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ef48bf4-b61d-5d18-8d06-67153f8f0864" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453172} {:answer/id #uuid "aead6e6b-ab86-52e2-ab5e-8e74bd9b4b5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453173}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aead6e6b-ab86-52e2-ab5e-8e74bd9b4b5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453173} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c719c4e-9fc3-558a-a32d-6604969ef25f" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454336}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "39b57e8a-5e0f-5758-8d6b-0d9667e7e35b" :question/math-academy-id "q-105258" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:R\\to R$ which is given by $f(x)={2}^{-x}?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The range of $f$ is $[0,\\infty )$\n\n- **II.** $∀\\,y\\in R,$ $∃\\,x\\in R$ such that $f(x)=y$\n\n- **III.** $f$ maps $R$ **into** $R$" :question/worked-solution "First, we graph the function.\n\n![](images/c7/c79c1123036c978c8c4da514651c0bb1c8e3df34c8bbaff099bee601d568ed10.png)\n\nRecall that $f:X\\to Y$ is an *into* function if it is not a surjection. In other words, there exists an element $y$ in $Y$ such that it has no preimage in $X:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is an into function if $∃\\,y\\in Y$ such that $∀\\,x\\in X,$ we have $f(x)\\ne y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. The graph will cover all $y$-values greater than $y=0$, excluding $y=0$ itself. So the range of the function is $(0,\\infty ).$\n\n- Statement II is false. Take, for example, $y=-1.$ Since the range of the function is $(0,\\infty ),$ there can't be an $x\\in R$ whose image is $-1.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is false, the function is not a surjection.  So, $f$ maps $R$ *into* $R.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410011 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161921 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "01ad9700-5aaa-5b00-8d2f-acce6ed59c9a" :knowledge-point/title "Functions Whose Codomain Is the Set of Real Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9f4b9fce-88a2-5c65-8752-31bb8c08b10d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454090} {:answer/id #uuid "1c77a378-a0f8-5768-8e57-d661a10c42dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454091}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9f4b9fce-88a2-5c65-8752-31bb8c08b10d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454090} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae3c14ef-feb4-50b1-b173-09d5116caffe" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454795} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6fd58017-e4ba-5b47-983d-1e652dcc9e5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454092} {:answer/id #uuid "d49b29d6-d5d4-51be-84b7-33db7b3b848e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454093}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d49b29d6-d5d4-51be-84b7-33db7b3b848e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454093} :answer-field/id #uuid "35de4aba-fc6c-5fa8-a181-9eb17458aad4" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454796} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00096cbf-a739-5274-b425-3e305c30dad4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454094} {:answer/id #uuid "80dd2edb-196d-5524-841f-8e00d6c94a8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454095}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "00096cbf-a739-5274-b425-3e305c30dad4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454094} :answer-field/id #uuid "df7bb5e2-b8b1-56ec-86e5-324f98f8a216" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454797}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4110bb56-279f-50bf-96a1-301ebf1eb3ce" :question/math-academy-id "q-90859" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:(0,\\infty )\\to R$ which is given by $f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The range of $f$ is $(0,\\infty )$\n\n- **II.** $∀\\,y\\in R$ $∃\\,x\\in (0,\\infty )$ such that $f(x)=y$\n\n- **III.** $f$ maps $(0,\\infty )$ **into** $R$" :question/worked-solution "First, we graph the function.\n\n![](images/5e/5e3e074a2d029aeb3f4016332b9fb762fff6ec60ed7dce0290f97a95d6cb57c1.png)\n\nRecall that $f:X\\to Y$ is an *into* function if it is not a surjection. In other words, there exists an element $y$ in $Y$ such that it has no preimage in $X:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is an into function if $∃\\,y\\in Y$ such that $∀\\,x\\in X,$ we have $f(x)\\ne y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. From the graph, there is no highest or lowest $y$ value. The graph will cover any real value $y.$ So the range of the function is all $R..$\n\n- Statement II is true. Since the range of the function is $(-\\infty ,\\infty )$, then for all $y$ contained within $(-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ there exists some $x$ contained within $R$ such that $f(x)=y.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since the range of the function is $(-\\infty ,\\infty )$ the function is a surjection. Therefore, $f$ is *not* an into function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410012 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161922 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dd378899-03ff-57a0-848c-11b93c8e5055" :knowledge-point/title "Functions Whose Codomain Is a Real Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c93ca70a-47da-5baf-851c-e1bf791c7b9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453174} {:answer/id #uuid "64807ced-aa57-58a5-ae0d-ac029c59ac34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453175}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "64807ced-aa57-58a5-ae0d-ac029c59ac34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453175} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b4fceb5-932c-5132-bb87-d2badbb9ddb9" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454337} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c61cf70-41be-5318-bf2e-74949ba6f18f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453176} {:answer/id #uuid "236cd33b-d523-510a-84cc-440d53a1b398" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453177}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6c61cf70-41be-5318-bf2e-74949ba6f18f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453176} :answer-field/id #uuid "39af1c63-d29d-5ade-b582-b9d3d244610e" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454338} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ef1019c-6076-59b2-b8b1-dfd04b1ded3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453178} {:answer/id #uuid "3d6c31df-bd28-538d-b442-6e9f77cc33df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453179}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2ef1019c-6076-59b2-b8b1-dfd04b1ded3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453178} :answer-field/id #uuid "5543a8bb-3812-58e8-8791-6e292fe8e1f3" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454339}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9b62af08-9109-5599-b006-f2ceb899c9fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-105263" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:R\\to (-\\infty ,1)$ which is given by $f(x)=1-{2}^{x}?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The range of $f$ is $(-\\infty ,1)$\n\n- **II.** $∀\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,1],$ $∃\\,x\\in R$ such that $f(x)=y$\n\n- **III.** $f$ is a function of $R$ **into** $(-\\infty ,1)$" :question/worked-solution "First, we graph the function.\n\n![](images/35/35bd21eef06d1ea63aba6e420d9842de61f9248c4fa26c2895f6825f4e7a3848.png)\n\nRecall that $f:X\\to Y$ is an *into* function if it is not a surjection. In other words, there exists an element $y$ in $Y$ such that it has no preimage in $X:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is an into function if $∃\\,y\\in Y$ such that $∀\\,x\\in X,$ we have $f(x)\\ne y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. From the graph, the function takes all $y$-values lower than $y=1$, excluding $y=1$ itself. So the range of the function is indeed $(-\\infty ,1).$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since the range of the function is $(-\\infty ,1)$,  there can't be an $x\\in R$ whose image is $1\\notin (-\\infty ,1).$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement I is true, the function is a surjection.  So, $f$ is *not* a function of $R$ *into* $(-\\infty ,1).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410545 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119845 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8a5d11c2-4a7c-5fdc-a363-8a87b90db19e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Dimension of a Span by Inspection"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ae48163-0998-5b3d-b29e-8d844bd75e73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453454} {:answer/id #uuid "fac7d0b5-081a-56e0-901b-a2ae495d04aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453455}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3ae48163-0998-5b3d-b29e-8d844bd75e73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453454} :answer-field/id #uuid "d31b9f46-6bca-5c00-88d4-25fd24f38387" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454477} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f8a92446-e8c8-5739-82ef-d0ba00e62ae7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453456} {:answer/id #uuid "00c70672-536d-5c0e-84ab-327beb9e056e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453457}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "00c70672-536d-5c0e-84ab-327beb9e056e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453457} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d6e49be-3808-5326-8880-c9624d3a62b4" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454478} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d46f9ac4-f8c7-5cc1-9675-07387c704c56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453458} {:answer/id #uuid "325a6d83-0f48-5758-9374-3733e1e6f1c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453459}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d46f9ac4-f8c7-5cc1-9675-07387c704c56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453458} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ea1fc63-07a4-50e6-a7e4-57b3bf645806" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454479}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6a087057-8a12-50fd-9bce-b13921276b0f" :question/math-academy-id "q-159782" :question/problem "Let ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}$ be linearly independent vectors, and suppose that the vector $w$ can be written as a linear combination of ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${v}_{1},{v}_{2}$ form a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}\\}$\n\n- **II.** $\\text{dim}(\\text{Span}\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},w\\})=2$\n\n- **III.** $\\text{dim}(\\text{Span}\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}\\})=2$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a basis of a vector space $V$ is a set of linearly independent vectors that span $V.$ The dimension of $V$ is the number of vectors in any basis of $V$ (if such a basis exists). \n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed, $\\text{Span}\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}\\}$ is spanned by ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}$, and we are told that ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}$ are linearly independent vectors. So, ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}$ is a basis of the span.\n\n- Statement II is true. We are told that $w$ can be written as a linear combination of ${v}_{1},{v}_{2}.$ This means that $\\text{Span}\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},w\\}$ is completely spanned by the vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2}$ only. So, $\\text{dim}(\\text{Span}\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},w\\})=2.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Indeed, $\\text{Span}\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}\\}$ is spanned by ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}$, and we are told that ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}$ are linearly independent vectors. So, ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}$ is a basis of the span. Therefore, we have $\\text{dim}(\\text{Span}\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}\\})=3$ (not $2$).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411065 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059689 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0d56b033-a2c8-57c7-adde-e574d726ec78" :knowledge-point/title "Rewriting Symbolic Conditional Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e80d5d8d-2b17-5886-9b55-a7b81e348575" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453622} {:answer/id #uuid "eb698ee6-4b77-5b14-90cb-e74df6b1abac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453623}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb698ee6-4b77-5b14-90cb-e74df6b1abac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453623} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ab0edef-ad32-52ce-a777-7ef518d62f83" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454561} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d8de87b1-d8ef-50e0-94f7-a2832adb4959" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453624} {:answer/id #uuid "f7312739-063d-5aef-8534-6f2ac7974c84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453625}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d8de87b1-d8ef-50e0-94f7-a2832adb4959" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453624} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9edf5f2-ac8c-5b69-99b2-3ae4c084b126" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454562} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54641cb5-3584-597c-bcb0-67da0251b5b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453626} {:answer/id #uuid "8a7d916c-501c-57d8-ad96-61e5a1dc8fde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453627}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8a7d916c-501c-57d8-ad96-61e5a1dc8fde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453627} :answer-field/id #uuid "a2b4fa69-fdf7-5386-8328-31ecb2099e55" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454563}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c7ec246a-1c3b-5830-ae08-ed99cbcc20da" :question/math-academy-id "q-182503" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A⇒B≡¬A∨B$\n- **II.** $¬(A⇒B)≡A∨¬B$\n- **III.** $¬(A⇒B)≡A∧¬B$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of our statements:\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, $A⇒B$ is logically equivalent to the disjunction $¬A∨B.$\n\n- Statement III is true, while statement II is false. From part I, we have the following equivalence:\n\n$$\nA⇒B≡¬A∨B\n$$\n\nBy negating this statement, we get\n\n$$\n¬(A⇒B)≡¬(¬A∨B).\n$$\n\nDistributing the negation over the disjunction using De Morgan's law, we have\n\n$$\n¬(¬A∨B)≡¬(¬A)∧¬B.\n$$\n\nCanceling out double negation, we reach\n\n$$\nA∧¬B.\n$$\n\nSo, $¬(A⇒B)$ is equivalent to $A∧¬B.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411415 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157237 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8479a60b-b5db-5ad4-8100-fd2db8002091" :knowledge-point/title "Using the x R y Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d941faec-e94f-51c2-a015-6e9922022b3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453700} {:answer/id #uuid "6cf7c851-e652-5e8e-8a5f-aea78dae8d9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453701}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6cf7c851-e652-5e8e-8a5f-aea78dae8d9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453701} :answer-field/id #uuid "33241716-9c2f-5527-9caf-28ca41203246" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454600} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6d75d6d2-7386-5acc-ad1a-1337eec447d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453702} {:answer/id #uuid "5e5651d3-07d9-555a-b807-433068b6fa9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453703}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d75d6d2-7386-5acc-ad1a-1337eec447d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453702} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb50187f-3fd4-55dd-96b1-59e3e5d83fb4" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454601} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9171ea78-358f-5962-92c7-ee1e5b63f94e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453704} {:answer/id #uuid "b1018595-c01c-5712-a26d-4c1d47390d3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453705}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9171ea78-358f-5962-92c7-ee1e5b63f94e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453704} :answer-field/id #uuid "6937c55d-93a2-573c-bbc0-83804147eb3e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454602}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5fbac889-73d0-5b8f-a301-da4ef8cb327a" :question/math-academy-id "q-213127" :question/problem "Consider the following set:\n\n$$\nA={1,3}\n$$\n\nGiven the relation $R$ on $A$ defined by\n\n$$\nx\\,R\\,y\\,⇔\\,x=y,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $1\\,R\\,1$\n- **II.** $1\\,R\\,3$\n- **III.** $3\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,3$" :question/worked-solution "A relation $R$ on a set $A$ is a subset of the Cartesian product $A\\times A={A}^{2}.$\n\n$$\nR⊆{A}^{2}\n$$\n\nWe also have the following notations:\n\n- $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $(x,y)\\in R$\n\n- $x\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,y$ if and only if $(x,y)\\notin R$\n\nIn this case, we have $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $x=y.$ For this relation, note that\n\n- the symbols $R$ and $=$ are interchangeable, and\n\n- the symbols $\\cancel{\\,R\\,}$ and $\\ne $ are also interchangeable.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn:\n\n- Statement I is  true. Replacing $R$ with the symbol $=$, we have $1=1,$ which is true.\n\n- Statement II is false. Replacing $R$ with the symbol $=,$ we have $1=3,$ which is false.\n\n- Statement III is false. Replacing $\\cancel{\\,R\\,}$ with the symbol $\\ne ,$ we have $3\\ne 3,$ which is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411416 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157237 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8479a60b-b5db-5ad4-8100-fd2db8002091" :knowledge-point/title "Using the x R y Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5be660f9-b1a6-5c44-a236-1528e3ac5e2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453706} {:answer/id #uuid "633efbab-1e9c-519d-8c87-cf31633aa603" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453707}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5be660f9-b1a6-5c44-a236-1528e3ac5e2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453706} :answer-field/id #uuid "efb6a831-307e-5cc1-8685-62da4be3c7f2" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454603} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fe94c89-0c24-5c68-b631-7696e034ff88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453708} {:answer/id #uuid "f9b2dd14-66fb-53c2-8cc1-84b717d05aae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453709}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f9b2dd14-66fb-53c2-8cc1-84b717d05aae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453709} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8465c33-c520-5083-bc54-d81a74f17a81" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454604} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6f47a411-e333-573c-987e-13415220e695" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453710} {:answer/id #uuid "17e30408-772b-5358-b7a6-03830f24a9aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453711}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "17e30408-772b-5358-b7a6-03830f24a9aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453711} :answer-field/id #uuid "b62f52a8-c0a4-55c9-8e09-ccce1ff6f34f" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454605}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "77fae439-40b7-5f50-94ed-61df5583b377" :question/math-academy-id "q-213144" :question/problem "Consider the following set:\n\n$$\nA={2,4,6}\n$$\n\nGiven the relation $R$ on $A$ defined by\n\n$$\nx\\,R\\,y\\,⇔\\,x∤y,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $2\\,R\\,4$\n- **II.** $4\\,R\\,6$\n- **III.** $2\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,6$" :question/worked-solution "A relation $R$ on a set $A$ is a subset of the Cartesian product $A\\times A={A}^{2}.$\n\n$$\nR⊆{A}^{2}\n$$\n\nWe also have the following notations:\n\n- $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $(x,y)\\in R$\n\n- $x\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,y$ if and only if $(x,y)\\notin R$\n\nIn this case, we have $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $x∤y.$ For this relation, note that\n\n- the symbols $R$ and $∤$ are interchangeable, and\n\n- the symbols $\\cancel{\\,R\\,}$ and $∣$ are also interchangeable.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn:\n\n- Statement I is false. Replacing $R$ with the symbol $∤$, we have $2∤4,$ which is false.\n\n- Statement II is true. Replacing $R$ with the symbol $∤,$ we have $4∤6,$ which is true.\n\n- Statement III is true. Replacing $\\cancel{\\,R\\,}$ with the symbol $∣,$ we have $2∣6,$ which is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411423 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157237 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8479a60b-b5db-5ad4-8100-fd2db8002091" :knowledge-point/title "Using the x R y Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35885383-bf11-52c5-ba9d-4f4b1185ebb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453712} {:answer/id #uuid "3f1f43dd-5919-53ae-a648-3a99f59c4a22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453713}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f1f43dd-5919-53ae-a648-3a99f59c4a22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453713} :answer-field/id #uuid "20de8fe4-991c-5757-87fe-b795e35d4479" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454606} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d8f51057-de81-5138-a23d-33ea78923c97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453714} {:answer/id #uuid "00dd75c6-eea2-5a86-bfe5-3fdbc213e543" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453715}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "00dd75c6-eea2-5a86-bfe5-3fdbc213e543" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453715} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e28ba17-46e7-5a69-aeb0-17ccae0ab090" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454607} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d922689-7ef7-5604-8706-8851f69b6923" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453716} {:answer/id #uuid "f5fc08b8-39cf-571a-8ab5-29a1d31aa564" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453717}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1d922689-7ef7-5604-8706-8851f69b6923" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453716} :answer-field/id #uuid "a7423bc3-695e-500a-99f4-aadd8e9ace7b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454608}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e3479154-8b81-59b7-8f1a-b3765342f61c" :question/math-academy-id "q-213145" :question/problem "Consider the following set:\n\n$$\nA={1,2}\n$$\n\nGiven the relation $R$ on $A$ defined by\n\n$$\nx\\,R\\,y\\,⇔\\,x∣y,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $1\\,R\\,1$\n- **II.** $1\\,R\\,2$\n- **III.** $2\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,2$" :question/worked-solution "A relation $R$ on a set $A$ is a subset of the Cartesian product $A\\times A={A}^{2}.$\n\n$$\nR⊆{A}^{2}\n$$\n\nWe also have the following notations:\n\n- $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $(x,y)\\in R$\n\n- $x\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,y$ if and only if $(x,y)\\notin R$\n\nIn this case, we have $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $x∣y.$ For this relation, note that\n\n- the symbols $R$ and $∣$ are interchangeable, and\n\n- the symbols $\\cancel{\\,R\\,}$ and $∤$ are also interchangeable.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. Replacing $R$ with the symbol $∣$, we have $1∣1,$ which is true.\n\n- Statement II is true. Replacing $R$ with the symbol $∣,$ we have $1∣2,$ which is true.\n\n- Statement III is false. Replacing $\\cancel{\\,R\\,}$ with the symbol $∤,$ we have $2∤2,$ which is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411427 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157237 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8479a60b-b5db-5ad4-8100-fd2db8002091" :knowledge-point/title "Using the x R y Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid 