e {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453687}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5b5358be-8415-5ad4-ad47-03138a3beabd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453686} :answer-field/id #uuid "47ef3334-aefa-55ba-981a-899122d87488" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454593}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "579647d8-78b0-511b-8a94-882ec6fc1b22" :question/math-academy-id "q-212923" :question/problem "Given the relation $R$ on $N$ defined by\n\n$$\nx\\,R\\,y\\,⇔\\,x>y,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $6\\,R\\,8$\n\n- **II.** $7\\,R\\,2$\n\n- **III.** $9\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,1$" :question/worked-solution "A relation $R$ on a set $A$ is a subset of the Cartesian product $A\\times A={A}^{2}.$\n\n$$\nR⊆A\\times A\n$$\n\nWe also have the following notations:\n\n- $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $(x,y)\\in R$\n\n- $x\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,y$ if and only if $(x,y)\\notin R$\n\nIn this case, we have $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $x>y.$ For this relation, note that\n\n- the symbols $R$ and $>$ are interchangeable, and\n\n- the symbols $\\cancel{\\,R\\,}$ and $≯$ (or, equivalently, $\\cancel{\\,R\\,}$ and $\\le $) are also interchangeable.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn:\n\n- Statement I is false. Replacing $R$ with the symbol $>,$ we have $6>8,$ which is false.\n\n- Statement II is true. Replacing $R$ with the symbol $>,$ we have $7>2,$ which is true.\n\n- Statement III is false. Replacing $\\cancel{\\,R\\,}$ with the symbol $\\le ,$ we have $9\\le 1,$ which is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411678 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203899 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff71f3f5-8383-5815-ba42-289f14e16b57" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Ordered Pairs Belonging to a Standard Relation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8587e734-006d-527c-a8c8-73090b97f285" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453688} {:answer/id #uuid "982f7ef5-cc7e-5bf7-b407-84e014e93125" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453689}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8587e734-006d-527c-a8c8-73090b97f285" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453688} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d106978-3825-5783-b82f-260e5e09a3b0" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454594} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e259bb54-f7de-5f20-98e7-eb69df3da9f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453690} {:answer/id #uuid "875ac699-118d-533e-b443-208590e44f69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453691}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e259bb54-f7de-5f20-98e7-eb69df3da9f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453690} :answer-field/id #uuid "3afd2430-2118-5392-b5f4-b679fd87253d" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454595} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f51b0a65-f7e4-568e-89be-e3f7bb38c80c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value 