045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453698} {:answer/id #uuid "75097d40-93bc-5fc9-9154-d423738c8e60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453699}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "75097d40-93bc-5fc9-9154-d423738c8e60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453699} :answer-field/id #uuid "5e55a813-df68-5a59-b03e-aaafd1e0f4b6" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454599}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b5b2a52b-fd77-5422-b1dc-3a9ca690060e" :question/math-academy-id "q-212983" :question/problem "Given the relation $R$ on $Z$ defined by\n\n$$\nx\\,R\\,y\\,⇔\\,x≡y+4\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6),\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $0\\,R\\,2$\n\n- **II.** $1\\,R\\,9$\n\n- **III.** $4\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,13$" :question/worked-solution "A relation $R$ on a set $A$ is a subset of the Cartesian product $A\\times A={A}^{2}.$\n\n$$\nR⊆A\\times A\n$$\n\nWe also have the following notations:\n\n- $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $(x,y)\\in R$\n\n- $x\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,y$ if and only if $(x,y)\\notin R$\n\nIn this case, we have $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $x≡y+4\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6),$ or equivalently, $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $6∣(x-y-4).$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. In this case, we have $6∣(0-2-4),$ which is true.\n\n- Statement II is true. In this case, we have $6∣(1-9-4),$ which is true.\n\n- Statement III is true. In this case, we have $6∤(4-13-4),$ which is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411856 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162013 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c67d532-acd9-5231-a27f-d39084863e01" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Spectral Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "577c6459-a68e-5617-9007-38fe998472ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454202} {:answer/id #uuid "9803254f-68b7-5b7e-936e-f2b01fcb4624" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454203}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "577c6459-a68e-5617-9007-38fe998472ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454202} :answer-field/id #uuid "40924b97-51ec-57fe-9300-e75dc6817c4c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454851} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d6225d8-02a3-5861-9a49-a929038a7ee8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454204} {:answer/id #uuid "b251d743-a66c-5bae-a8cf-5ca14a90f254" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454205}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3d6225d8-02a3-5861-9a49-a929038a7ee8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454204} :answer-field/id #uuid "6cae005c-ab57-5373-a6f8-1aefd15ba7ba" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454852} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c7230c31-5927-5a08-a14e-0066312e17b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454206} {:answer/id #uuid "98cbb68b-2336-539d-bb6a-8b6710f91c0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454207}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98cbb68b-2336-539d-bb6a-8b6710f91c0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454207} :answer-field/id #uuid "e249821b-901a-5fb1-b815-d0984e6c7c99" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454853}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "409399cd-9cd7-53bb-83f5-ffa99003572c" :question/math-academy-id "q-95407" :question/problem "Given that $A$ is a real symmetric matrix, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A$ must have a complex eigenvalue\n\n- **II.** $A$ is not diagonalizable\n\n- **III.** If $u$ and $v$ are two eigenvectors corresponding to different eigenvalues, then $u⊥v$" :question/worked-solution "Given that $A$ is an $n\\times n$ symmetric matrix over $R$, the spectral theorem states the following:\n\n- The eigenvalues of $A$ are all real.\n\n- Eigenvectors corresponding to different eigenvalues are orthogonal.\n\n- The dimension of the eigenspace for each eigenvalue equals the multiplicity of that eigenvalue as a root of the characteristic polynomial.\n\n- $A$ is orthogonally diagonalizable.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. According to the spectral theorem, the eigenvalues are real.\n\n- Statement II is false. According to the spectral theorem, any symmetric matrix with real entries is orthogonally diagonalizable, so, $A$ is diagonalizable.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, eigenvectors corresponding to different eigenvalues must be orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412421 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115235 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9923c6c3-e425-54ae-a533-09421d5578cb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a True Statement Given a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "538e7fe6-b399-5899-a9f8-ecf6b1aae817" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453842} {:answer/id #uuid "ef9fecf5-e15f-5c9e-8512-53b3ec9864c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453843}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef9fecf5-e15f-5c9e-8512-53b3ec9864c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453843} :answer-field/id #uuid "b361575c-aa03-5dbf-b411-97171b912788" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454671} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98ef04fa-1c1c-50a2-bdbb-2d85ae96f31e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453844} {:answer/id #uuid "48b4ae45-27c7-56eb-8ab2-ae845aa073be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453845}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98ef04fa-1c1c-50a2-bdbb-2d85ae96f31e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453844} :answer-field/id #uuid "93942ac4-88b5-56a0-89a7-6a3ffa4986b0" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454672} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c36e8ab9-e979-5531-8a73-b3a76c58382b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453846} {:answer/id #uuid "145e9b16-dc59-5418-ac2c-92a5cf27033b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453847}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c36e8ab9-e979-5531-8a73-b3a76c58382b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453846} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c5d49d8-f8a3-5b1d-98ea-81d7fa4820c6" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454673}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "79c14c2f-568d-5ff3-b628-6c8dd8d0639f" :question/math-academy-id "q-32169" :question/problem "Let \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The lines $5x-4y=0$ and $x+2y=0$ intersect at exactly one point\n- **II.** ${A}^{-1}$ does **not** exist\n- **III.** $Ax=0$ has no solution" :question/worked-solution "Recall that given $A=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22}\\end{aligned}]$, then according to the invertible matrix theorem the following statements are equivalent:    \n\n- $A$ is invertible.\n\n- The system $Ax=b$ has exactly one solution for any $2\\times 1$ column vector $b.$\n\n- The system $Ax=0$ has the unique zero solution.\n\n- The lines ${a}_{11}x+{a}_{12}y={b}_{1}$ and ${a}_{21}x+{a}_{22}y={b}_{2}$ intersect at exactly one point.\n\n- $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\nNow, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =det[\\begin{aligned}5 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =5\\cdot 2-(-4)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =14\\ne 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since the fifth part of the invertible matrix theorem is true, all the other parts of the theorem are true too. \n\nWith that in mind, let's now check our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true by the fourth part of  the invertible matrix theorem.\n\n- Statement II is false by the first part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\n- Statement III is false. According to the third part of the invertible matrix theorem, the system $Ax=0$ has the unique zero solution.\n\nTherefore, only statement I is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412961 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152100 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d1a842b5-7256-59cd-b33f-d590bc315d84" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d90f90f5-3e74-572c-aa89-9724b4da180e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453988} {:answer/id #uuid "11a83033-f355-5373-a7f0-51d0ef965472" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453989}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d90f90f5-3e74-572c-aa89-9724b4da180e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453988} :answer-field/id #uuid "69f93893-49bf-50eb-9cb8-5100bc1b0a48" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454744} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "caafc5ae-8676-58f7-be01-e74b00b73515" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453990} {:answer/id #uuid "2dad5cff-3cef-5b95-a702-f2684708b692" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453991}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "caafc5ae-8676-58f7-be01-e74b00b73515" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453990} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf3b9fd7-6d29-582c-857b-0ed344345e75" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454745} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d2ebe3c7-2898-5c09-95a0-a9683da87a51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453992} {:answer/id #uuid "6cf20969-d67c-5204-9e7c-1a8067b679d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453993}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6cf20969-d67c-5204-9e7c-1a8067b679d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453993} :answer-field/id #uuid "471dce59-5681-5b77-b94e-7501e5f87b82" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454746}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0f9012f2-83ba-5f6f-b553-2ea47d5d4f81" :question/math-academy-id "q-78640" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** There are $3$ distinct residue classes modulo $6$\n\n- **II.** $[5]_{3}\\cap [1]_{3}\\ne ∅$\n\n- **III.** $Z=[3]_{2}\\cup [6]_{2}$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the residue classes modulo $n$ have the following properties:\n\n- There are exactly $n$ distinct residue classes modulo $n$\n\n- Two distinct residue classes have an empty intersection: $[a]_{n}\\cap [b]_{n}=∅$ if $a≢b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)$\n\n- Residue classes modulo $n$ form a partition of the set of all integers: \n\n$$\nZ=[0]_{n}\\cup [1]_{n}\\cup ⋯\\cup [n-1]_{n}\n$$\n\n- The integers modulo $n$ is defined as the set containing all distinct residue classes modulo $n$: \n\n$$\n{Z}_{n}=\\{[0]_{n},\\,[1]_{n},\\,…,\\,[n-1]_{n}\\}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's now consider each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. There are exactly $6$ distinct residue classes modulo $6.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $5≢1\\,(\\text{mod }3),$ we have that $[5]_{3}\\cap [1]_{3}=∅.$\n\n- Statement III is true. First, notice the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[3]_{2} & =[1+2\\cdot 1]_{2}=[1]_{2} \\\\ [6]_{2} & =[0+2\\cdot 3]_{2}=[0]_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[3]_{2}\\cup [6]_{2} & =[1]_{2}\\cup [0]_{2} \\\\  & =[0]_{2}\\cup [1]_{2} \\\\  & =Z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412977 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152100 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d1a842b5-7256-59cd-b33f-d590bc315d84" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "99c866b5-fa78-5463-879f-91c030b81919" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453994} {:answer/id #uuid "ed31939a-f058-5205-8c6b-722767e7b7c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453995}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed31939a-f058-5205-8c6b-722767e7b7c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453995} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9c2fd1a-fb98-5cd0-b399-c001871510bd" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454747} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e0d1411-6ced-5ae0-ac91-be6911cf7935" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453996} {:answer/id #uuid "4793bdef-ca97-5b0f-8ccf-abb72b491ceb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453997}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4793bdef-ca97-5b0f-8ccf-abb72b491ceb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453997} :answer-field/id #uuid "31727710-9d5d-5ec7-b533-3911fcb1abea" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454748} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "320480f6-35f8-534c-b475-8279339d8454" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453998} {:answer/id #uuid "6887d8ad-0703-528f-abc1-66d945caef6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453999}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6887d8ad-0703-528f-abc1-66d945caef6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453999} :answer-field/id #uuid "33f65df0-556a-5ca2-b14a-a5fd084c424a" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454749}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f68491fc-7fbf-551d-bb56-21bac80c159f" :question/math-academy-id "q-78644" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** There are $11$ distinct residue classes modulo $11$\n\n- **II.** $[7]_{5}\\cap [2]_{5}\\ne ∅$\n\n- **III.** $Z=[0]_{4}\\cup [9]_{4}\\cup [2]_{4}\\cup [15]_{4}$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the residue classes modulo $n$ have the following properties:\n\n- There are exactly $n$ distinct residue classes modulo $n$\n\n- Two distinct residue classes have an empty intersection: $[a]_{n}\\cap [b]_{n}=∅$ if $a≢b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)$\n\n- Residue classes modulo $n$ form a partition of the set of all integers: \n\n$$\nZ=[0]_{n}\\cup [1]_{n}\\cup ⋯\\cup [n-1]_{n}\n$$\n\n- The integers modulo $n$ is defined as the set containing all distinct residue classes modulo $n$: \n\n$$\n{Z}_{n}=\\{[0]_{n},\\,[1]_{n},\\,…,\\,[n-1]_{n}\\}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's now consider each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. There are $11$ distinct residue classes modulo $11.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, since $7≡2\\,(\\text{mod }5),$ we have that $[7]_{5}=[2]_{5}.$ Therefore, $[7]_{5}\\cap [2]_{5}\\ne ∅.$\n\n- Statement III is true. First, notice the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[9]_{4} & =[1+4\\cdot 2]_{4}=[1]_{4} \\\\ [15]_{4} & =[3+4\\cdot 3]_{4}=[3]_{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[0]_{4}\\cup [9]_{4}\\cup [2]_{4}\\cup [15]_{4} & =[0]_{4}\\cup [1]_{4}\\cup [2]_{4}\\cup [3]_{4} \\\\  & =Z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412998 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152225 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "04926916-8e08-5401-a57b-3fd333741913" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Generalized Eigenvectors Using Definition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8610a0d2-fdc1-5ffb-bb7d-fa4d5ec60050" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453246} {:answer/id #uuid "1106162e-004a-5376-84ea-4d09f59735a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453247}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1106162e-004a-5376-84ea-4d09f59735a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453247} :answer-field/id #uuid "16308504-1737-59ec-85f8-6aae9a6e62ca" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454373} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "654b12c7-247f-59a8-b59b-c9aa7e6df741" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453248} {:answer/id #uuid "d1caa7bb-f241-5fda-a091-982727ce423c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453249}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "654b12c7-247f-59a8-b59b-c9aa7e6df741" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453248} :answer-field/id #uuid "dec4b167-b790-52bb-b09f-3c495acb1957" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454374} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7fb38f24-ce58-5679-8e4c-5ab1475e60b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453250} {:answer/id #uuid "c9beb16d-fb59-5d8a-9e62-f88859d6a643" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453251}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c9beb16d-fb59-5d8a-9e62-f88859d6a643" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453251} :answer-field/id #uuid "291c74d0-3740-5390-9af2-8599a8ba49e9" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454375}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "28941d92-3462-55d4-9376-780e240021c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-109277" :question/problem "$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\overset{A+3I\\,}{\\to }v\\overset{A+3I\\,}{\\to }w\\overset{A+3I\\,}{\\to }0 \\\\ x\\overset{A-3I\\,}{\\to }y\\overset{A-3I\\,}{\\to }0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven the action of the matrices $A+3I$ and $A-3I$ on the nonzero vectors $u,v,w,x$ and $y$ as depicted above, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $v$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $2$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-3$ of $A$\n\n- **II.** $u$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $2$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-3$ of $A$\n\n- **III.** $y$ is an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =3$ of $A$" :question/worked-solution "A *generalized eigenvector* ${v}_{n}$ of rank $n$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda $ of a matrix $A$ is a nonzero vector such that\n\n$$\n{v}_{n}\\overset{A-\\lambda I\\,}{\\to }{v}_{n-1}\\overset{A-\\lambda I\\,}{\\to }…\\overset{A-\\lambda I\\,}{\\to }{v}_{1}\\overset{A-\\lambda I\\,}{\\to }0,\n$$\n\nwhere ${v}_{n-1},{v}_{n-2},…,{v}_{1}\\ne 0.$ An *eigenvector* is simply a generalized eigenvector of rank $1.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, since \n\n$$\nv\\overset{A+3I\\,}{\\to }w\\overset{A+3I\\,}{\\to }0,\n$$\n\ni.e. $A+3I$ maps $v$ to $0$ in $2$ steps, \nthe vector $v$ is a generalized  eigenvector of rank $2$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-3$ of $A.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since\n\n$$\nu\\overset{A+3I\\,}{\\to }v\\overset{A+3I\\,}{\\to }w\\overset{A+3I\\,}{\\to }0,\n$$\n\ni.e. $A+3I$ maps $u$ to $0$ in $3$ steps, \nthe vector $u$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $3,$ not $2.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, since\n\n$$\ny\\overset{A-3I\\,}{\\to }0,\n$$\n\ni.e. $A-3I$ maps $y$ to $0$ in $1$ step, \nthe vector $y$ is an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =3$ of $A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413000 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152225 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "04926916-8e08-5401-a57b-3fd333741913" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Generalized Eigenvectors Using Definition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c6b747f5-b6fd-5eba-ae77-a9174a9eb0e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453252} {:answer/id #uuid "52b890bf-1e84-54cf-9889-91651247a068" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453253}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "52b890bf-1e84-54cf-9889-91651247a068" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453253} :answer-field/id #uuid "43c1092e-91a4-5e66-9c90-37891305f270" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454376} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fc93c4a8-f3e6-52d8-9ef2-057cd1fd00b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453254} {:answer/id #uuid "9e356dd9-cc07-5fef-886f-0f4115f8b97a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453255}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fc93c4a8-f3e6-52d8-9ef2-057cd1fd00b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453254} :answer-field/id #uuid "4825cadc-9f85-54bd-99c2-cb4b67256536" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454377} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "604f4f38-dfc8-500b-b033-c1d586698b9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453256} {:answer/id #uuid "00d18245-d9fc-5c4f-8e90-f44ae94f6e70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453257}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "604f4f38-dfc8-500b-b033-c1d586698b9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453256} :answer-field/id #uuid "205d0d73-77db-5f0e-9eb3-e7a3ed04c9e4" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454378}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "eddb46c6-735a-5bdf-b2a2-b57344c5441a" :question/math-academy-id "q-109434" :question/problem "$$\n\\begin{aligned}s\\overset{A-4I\\,}{\\to }u\\overset{A-4I\\,}{\\to }v\\overset{A-4I\\,}{\\to }w\\overset{A-4I\\,}{\\to }0 \\\\ x\\overset{\\,\\,\\,A\\,\\,\\,\\,}{\\to }y\\overset{\\,\\,\\,A\\,\\,\\,\\,}{\\to }0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven the action of the matrices $A-4I$ and $A$ on the nonzero vectors $s,u,v,w,x$ and $y$ as depicted above, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $s$ is a generalized  eigenvector of rank $4$  corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =4$ of $A$\n- **II.** $x$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $1$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =0$ of $A$\n- **III.** $v$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $3$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =4$ of $A$" :question/worked-solution "A *generalized eigenvector* ${v}_{n}$ of rank $n$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda $ of a matrix $A$ is a nonzero vector such that\n\n$$\n{v}_{n}\\overset{A-\\lambda I\\,}{\\to }{v}_{n-1}\\overset{A-\\lambda I\\,}{\\to }…\\overset{A-\\lambda I\\,}{\\to }{v}_{1}\\overset{A-\\lambda I\\,}{\\to }0,\n$$\n\nwhere ${v}_{n-1},{v}_{n-2},…,{v}_{1}\\ne 0.$ An *eigenvector* is simply a generalized eigenvector of rank $1.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, since \n\n$$\ns\\overset{A-4I\\,}{\\to }u\\overset{A-4I\\,}{\\to }v\\overset{A-4I\\,}{\\to }w\\overset{A-4I\\,}{\\to }0,\n$$\n\ni.e. $A-4I$ maps $s$ to $0$ in $4$ steps, \nthe vector $s$ is an generalized eigenvector of rank $4$  corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =4$ of $A.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since\n\n$$\nx\\overset{\\,\\,\\,A\\,\\,\\,\\,}{\\to }y\\overset{\\,\\,\\,A\\,\\,\\,\\,}{\\to }0,\n$$\n\ni.e. $A=A-0I$ maps $x$ to $0$ in $2$ steps, \nthe vector $x$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $2,$ not $1.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since\n\n$$\nv\\overset{A-4I\\,}{\\to }w\\overset{A-4I\\,}{\\to }0,\n$$\n\ni.e. $A-4I$ maps $v$ to $0$ in $2$ steps, \nthe vector $v$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $2,$ not $3.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413394 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166962 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "544f5154-5213-5898-a45d-4546bc8004c8" :knowledge-point/title "Understanding the Periodic Extension of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d69c9191-c57b-5b40-996e-777a184d420f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453862} {:answer/id #uuid "8e937e18-ad9e-5187-bca2-d80188955602" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453863}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e937e18-ad9e-5187-bca2-d80188955602" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453863} :answer-field/id #uuid "aab8922e-9958-52a6-a909-10999fa1e976" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454681} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eb70ef1e-3935-56b9-8d61-37338f1abc9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453864} {:answer/id #uuid "69936ea4-5a61-553c-a841-0f8856c0048e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453865}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "69936ea4-5a61-553c-a841-0f8856c0048e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453865} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe49bd90-5b54-5fa2-af50-8f2dcd2530ea" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454682} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ccc571d-7d63-5a29-b24d-f2770276a3af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453866} {:answer/id #uuid "7853f114-0b0e-5904-b1fc-5803694d16fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453867}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7853f114-0b0e-5904-b1fc-5803694d16fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453867} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a801a5f-980e-5406-9300-a022a15791c4" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454683}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4d1f9132-9d3c-569e-af11-701e82cf296a" :question/math-academy-id "q-340515" :question/problem "Let $F(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)$ for $x\\in R.$ Suppose $f(x)$ is the $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ from $x\\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ to $x\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $f(x)=F(x)$ for all $x\\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$\n\n- **II.** $f(x)=F(x)$ for all $x\\in R$\n\n- **III.** $f(x+2\\pi )=f(x)$ for all $x\\in R$" :question/worked-solution "Since $f$ is the $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$-periodic extension of $F,$ we have \n\n- $f(x+\\frac{\\pi }{2})=f(x)$ for all $x\\in R,$ and\n\n- $f(x)=F(x)$ for all $x\\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. This is exactly the definition of $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$-periodicity:\n\n$$\nf(x)=F(x)\n$$\n\n \nfor all $x\\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$\n\n- Statement II is true. Notice that $F$ itself is $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$-periodic, because for any $x\\in R,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x+\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(x+\\frac{\\pi }{2})) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x+2\\pi ) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x) \\\\  & =F(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $F$ already satisfies the periodicity rule, the $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$-periodic extension agrees with $F$ everywhere, so $f(x)=F(x)$ for all $x\\in R.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $f$ has period $\\frac{\\pi }{2},$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x+2\\pi )=f(x+4\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2})=f(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413395 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166962 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "544f5154-5213-5898-a45d-4546bc8004c8" :knowledge-point/title "Understanding the Periodic Extension of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a5ad7ce-a85f-5146-b73d-5c45f8bd9216" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453856} {:answer/id #uuid "0d314fdc-6ea0-598d-907c-085dc1c84e06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453857}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0d314fdc-6ea0-598d-907c-085dc1c84e06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453857} :answer-field/id #uuid "43975daa-88ca-549f-9c10-9ddfb429828c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454678} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d38eed8e-9345-5eb0-ad4b-4cb3cb071b6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453858} {:answer/id #uuid "03d7439a-1e1f-5e9b-ba05-1b9e13ddc7ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453859}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d38eed8e-9345-5eb0-ad4b-4cb3cb071b6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453858} :answer-field/id #uuid "72dae627-5309-5b18-9260-7056c334cd57" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454679} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "be925691-ed91-5787-a733-cd76fa4329cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453860} {:answer/id #uuid "d9310b4e-b012-578f-8840-b20475d111f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453861}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be925691-ed91-5787-a733-cd76fa4329cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453860} :answer-field/id #uuid "0916c6fa-5ef9-5bab-8f27-693033e2a146" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454680}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e155a024-962b-5f82-95d5-406e9c9d0535" :question/math-academy-id "q-340506" :question/problem "Let $G(x)=x+1$ for $x\\in R.$ Suppose $g(x)$ is the $4$-periodic extension of $G(x)$ from $x\\in [0,4)$ to $x\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $g(x+8)=g(x)$ for all $x\\in R$\n\n- **II.** $g(x)=G(x)$ for all $x\\in R$\n\n- **III.** $g(x+2)=g(x)$ for all $x\\in R$" :question/worked-solution "Since $g$ is the $4$-periodic extension of $G,$ we have \n\n- $g(x+4)=g(x)$ for all $x\\in R,$ and\n\n- $g(x)=G(x)$ for all $x\\in [0,4).$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(x+8)=g((x+4)+4)=g(x+4)=g(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $x\\in R.$\n\n- Statement II is false. For example, take $x=5.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(5)=g(1+4)=g(1)=G(1)=2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhile\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}G(5)=5+1=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $g(x)\\ne G(x)$ for $x=5.$\n\n- Statement III is false. For example, take $x=1.$ Then, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(1+2)=g(3)=G(3)=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhile \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(1)=G(1)=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $g(x+2)\\ne g(x)$ for $x=1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413744 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147427 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a19140af-1870-5dee-86a2-6052451803d4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intersection of Two Planes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a139c706-0e77-54a4-accb-bfe443670e5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453922} {:answer/id #uuid "f7a0a00e-bd44-522f-87a0-1661c0717d26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453923}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a139c706-0e77-54a4-accb-bfe443670e5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453922} :answer-field/id #uuid "227c754c-4dc6-54d5-bd20-dc203c3bd56d" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454711} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86a8ed31-2bd6-5da1-bce7-520c67f0b586" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453924} {:answer/id #uuid "7ef7da89-3321-5d51-9ea4-d7214de7dcff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453925}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7ef7da89-3321-5d51-9ea4-d7214de7dcff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453925} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d5956ce-b17c-56a5-9c55-441171fc7b01" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454712} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c079efb-b705-50e6-8fa4-f8d29cbaf064" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453926} {:answer/id #uuid "313e94f5-659f-51cb-b0fd-10e36f25ce06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453927}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6c079efb-b705-50e6-8fa4-f8d29cbaf064" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453926} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf7ace9d-04e4-53a1-8f3e-3670bba92643" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454713}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "abe7bafd-4069-5c23-9e34-e0cbd57e3732" :question/math-academy-id "q-71465" :question/problem "Given the two planes $x+y+z=0$ and $x+y+1=0$, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $⟨1,1,0⟩.$\n\n- **II.** The planes intersect on a line.\n\n- **III.** The planes are coincident." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $x+y+z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨1,1,1⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $x+y+1=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨1,1,0⟩.$\n\nNow, let's consider the statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed, computing the cross product of the normal vectors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨1,1,1⟩\\times ⟨1,1,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-i+j \\\\  & =⟨-1,1,0⟩\\ne ⟨1,1,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Since ${n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2}\\ne 0$, the vectors ${n}_{1}$ and ${n}_{2}$ are not parallel. Hence, the corresponding planes must intersect on a line.\n\n- Statement III is false. Indeed, two non-parallel planes could not be coincident either.\n\nTherefore, only statement II is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414417 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171919 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "308a8c68-628a-522f-9545-17a7165aefdf" :knowledge-point/title "Finite Vs. Infinite Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8164409b-fc2f-56e4-92d4-a571bd078853" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453598} {:answer/id #uuid "eeb1f6d0-b222-5b3f-9baa-7c642ab86cce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453599}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eeb1f6d0-b222-5b3f-9baa-7c642ab86cce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453599} :answer-field/id #uuid "a40cf449-4fd4-5e64-9d70-848e695dd9f7" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454549} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17bcd544-780e-5190-a922-8fdce92016c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453600} {:answer/id #uuid "758f338f-b7c9-5899-b704-a64a4557cdca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453601}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "17bcd544-780e-5190-a922-8fdce92016c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453600} :answer-field/id #uuid "5296953e-f85a-576d-85e5-e8e66679c838" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454550} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7466207f-97a3-5468-bf97-ceeb80781824" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453602} {:answer/id #uuid "e7dd3323-7ce5-5c2d-92b6-f2b7326e0e02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453603}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e7dd3323-7ce5-5c2d-92b6-f2b7326e0e02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453603} :answer-field/id #uuid "14d165f3-6a03-519c-af01-cefd1289cdbb" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454551}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1261accc-9253-5b2b-9450-d1cf9dd3a558" :question/math-academy-id "q-181624" :question/problem "$$\nX=\\{a,b,2,4\\},\\,Y=\\{n\\in N∣\\,1\\le n<5\\}\n$$\n\nConsider the sets $X$ and $Y$ given above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $|X|=4$\n\n- **II.** $|Y|=5$\n\n- **III.** $|X|=|Y|$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that finite sets have the same cardinality if and only if they have the same number of elements.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, $X$ is a finite set and $|X|=4.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Notice that $Y=\\{1,2,3,4\\}$ is a finite set and $|Y|=4.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, $X$ and $Y$ are finite sets and  $|X|=|Y|=4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414421 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171919 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "308a8c68-628a-522f-9545-17a7165aefdf" :knowledge-point/title "Finite Vs. Infinite Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f4a6a196-cf6f-52f0-8045-af9ff9cb5144" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453604} {:answer/id #uuid "742d1d8a-016b-5906-b5da-c25348b65e17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453605}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "742d1d8a-016b-5906-b5da-c25348b65e17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453605} :answer-field/id #uuid "b892b266-1449-568d-8bbc-3c7e3a9902e2" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454552} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d770434-e956-5fd5-ac23-3f91041ba568" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453606} {:answer/id #uuid "cb7b10d8-e60d-54d0-98b5-dc2a5e8d79f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453607}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4d770434-e956-5fd5-ac23-3f91041ba568" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453606} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e33b855-ffb8-5db0-9909-7903f8bb7381" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454553} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60e15853-0459-5bf5-84b7-84aad7819a3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453608} {:answer/id #uuid "7ef1f834-7372-5212-8d62-32d81d18248e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453609}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60e15853-0459-5bf5-84b7-84aad7819a3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453608} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac362871-d35a-50d9-94f6-dac624d013ad" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454554}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4c2743b2-72ab-5576-b421-aa5dcedd6c11" :question/math-academy-id "q-181626" :question/problem "$$\nS=\\{1,1,2,3,\\{4,5\\}\\},\\,T=\\{n\\in N∣\\,2\\le n\\le 7\\}\n$$\n\nConsider the sets $S$ and $T$ given above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $|S|=4$\n\n- **II.** $|T|=5$\n\n- **III.** $|S|=|T|$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that finite sets have the same cardinality if and only if they have the same number of elements.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed,  $S$ is a finite set and $|S|=4.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Notice that $T=\\{2,3,4,5,6,7\\}$ is a finite set and $|T|=6.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $4\\ne 6,$ we conclude that $|S|\\ne |T|.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415041 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152096 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3822141e-3cea-5c34-b925-a522c2273335" :knowledge-point/title "Combining the Division Properties"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a098b51-5864-5267-905d-b4179296f2cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453724} {:answer/id #uuid "dde9f7c7-a9c9-5819-8673-6787cab0e032" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453725}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5a098b51-5864-5267-905d-b4179296f2cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453724} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb6eb18b-ebbe-5e47-936e-bc1308655ecd" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454612} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aeac7296-f368-53b2-8209-e78e1cbe03ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453726} {:answer/id #uuid "79f2a3eb-3336-5dc7-94e3-e46fdf5da515" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453727}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "79f2a3eb-3336-5dc7-94e3-e46fdf5da515" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453727} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e29bc66-2a37-55e0-987d-f7b64c8332d9" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454613} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "522e6125-fc4c-592a-a8c0-86cb2d0f09f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453728} {:answer/id #uuid "fdc5c4c6-d7c5-5f71-92e0-98e3a1ed25cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453729}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fdc5c4c6-d7c5-5f71-92e0-98e3a1ed25cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453729} :answer-field/id #uuid "16c051c0-859a-5993-b80a-7c7f23db8490" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454614}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "00e9a03d-cb25-5bd2-bcfe-67d16e1b93d4" :question/math-academy-id "q-213297" :question/problem "Given that $5a≡5b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,15),$ which of the following statements **must** be true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6)$\n\n- **II.** $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,3)$\n\n- **III.** $4a≡4b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,12)$" :question/worked-solution "The division properties of modular arithmetic state the following:\n\n- For $k\\ne 0,$ we have\n\n$$\nka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,kn)\\,⟺\\,a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n).\n$$\n\n- For $\\text{gcd}(k,n)=1,$ we have \n\n$$\nka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n).\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false, while statement II is true. Applying the first property, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5a & ≡5b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,15) \\\\ 5\\cdot a & ≡5\\cdot b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,5\\cdot 3) \\\\ \\cancel{5}\\cdot a & ≡\\cancel{5}\\cdot b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,\\cancel{5}\\cdot 3) \\\\ a & ≡b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. By statement II and the first property, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,3)\\,⟺\\,4a≡4b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,12)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\n.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415043 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152094 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bca70f6c-d087-5b8e-aff2-581adca9ed1f" :knowledge-point/title "Using the First Division Property"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "351e928c-e004-5b10-b4b4-6fbeaec3e674" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453108} {:answer/id #uuid "e0c2c4cb-8526-52e7-8530-7f4ef0205cd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453109}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e0c2c4cb-8526-52e7-8530-7f4ef0205cd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453109} :answer-field/id #uuid "83e95d9e-5791-5b64-99df-1304941ab839" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454304} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0207b25f-bd59-5231-a62b-6725dad0da78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453110} {:answer/id #uuid "63421e5e-3260-591f-82be-4e744caa35d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453111}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0207b25f-bd59-5231-a62b-6725dad0da78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453110} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d959f59-bed8-52bf-b190-b4903555491f" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454305} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b9351d3-fa14-5e23-9460-be14c77c8dec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453112} {:answer/id #uuid "a1cc45f7-628e-5414-a635-a8b1f1b548a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453113}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1b9351d3-fa14-5e23-9460-be14c77c8dec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453112} :answer-field/id #uuid "a50f9674-ac44-5d4a-960a-fba84b9592c0" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454306}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0ff193af-a6fe-56c6-94b7-27cf32c1ffe5" :question/math-academy-id "q-103191" :question/problem "Given that $6a≡6b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,9),$ which of the following statements **must** be true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $2a≡2b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,3)$\n\n- **II.** $3a≡3b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6)$\n\n- **III.** $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,9)$" :question/worked-solution "The division property of modular arithmetic states that for $k\\ne 0,$ we have\n\n$$\nka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,kn)\\,⟺\\,a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n).\n$$\n\nWe're asked to consider the following statement:\n\n$$\n6a≡6b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,9)\n$$\n\nNotice that $\\text{gcd}(6,9)=3.$\n\nApplying the division property, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6a & ≡6b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,9) \\\\ 3\\cdot 2\\cdot a & ≡3\\cdot 2\\cdot b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,3\\cdot 3) \\\\ \\cancel{3}\\cdot 2\\cdot a & ≡\\cancel{3}\\cdot 2\\cdot b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,\\cancel{3}\\cdot 3) \\\\ 2a & ≡2b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"."}]}
